{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic","id":1349104,"title":"Scientific mystic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-17T09:55:29-08:00","id":1349104,"title":"Scientific mystic","content":"Do all mystics see what they are doing as magick? And all Etherite/VA and technocrats view their effects as Science? <br /> <br /> The Hermetics are a very study, scientific method based tradition. It is said they take apprentices, from military, halls of academia and scientific communities. They have a very structured approach to how magick works and study its behaviour since the beginning of the tradition, being the first ones to classify the 9 spheres.<br /> While they are considered mystics, they seem to put a lot of importance in science.<br /> <br /> &quot;Any sufficiently advanced science can be considered magick&quot; and vice-versa. So, if a science oriented mystic that knows why and how his magick work and can explain scientifically his effects is a mage or a scientist? Is he doing Science! or magick? I find it hard to separate those definitions, and while I know they are the same, the rules of M20 is different for both...<br /> <br /> <br /> So, I have an example character that kinda blends both views. I'd like opinions where he fits better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He's an electrical engineer really focused in his physical development as much as his mental. He is a very determined person and somewhat competitive, even a little bit egoistic and sometimes aggressive. Before awakening, he was always perfecting his body and mind. He did that by working out and practicing martial arts to get the best of his physical abilities, and meditating/studying to keep his mind sharp, always eager for more knowledge.<br /> After his awake, one more goal was added to his list: to obtain as more magickal power and knowledge as possible. His paradigm is &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot; with a bit of &quot;Might is Right&quot; and maybe &quot;Counsciousness is the only true reality&quot;: basically, he believes that Reality is unknown and changeable, product of our own beliefs. He believes that the act of believing, using your counsciousness and your Will, you can change reality according to your desire. His practices are Martial Arts, Chaos Magick and Psionics. He believes that there is an energy field, a force, not known to sleeper science, that binds everything together and is present everywhere. Much like the famous Chi, The Force, or Quintessence. This energy can be used, in conjunction of your Will, to affect the real world. How do he use it?<br /> With Energy, Gestures, Meditation, Eye Contact, Weapons, Books/Scrolls/Periodicals and Devices/Machines (dropped). Being a man of science, at first he tried to understand and learn more about this &quot;Force&quot; by doing experiments and trying to apply scientific methods to measure and describe it. He could only touch it with some devices that reacted to it. But as he discovered more about it, and the notion that Reality is changeable according to one's Will, he began to use his own body as an instrument to gather that energy and focus it according to his Will. Through research, he discovered that he no longer need any device to tap that energy (Arete 3 dropped instrument), because it is his conscience that is driving that energy into an effect. So, he rellies in his well built body to cast his spells.<br /> But, he didn't completely discarded his old methods. He is still a scientist and everything he does has a good scientifically explanation. Meditation/gestures change the brain and body activating certain areas that allows him to better tap that energy, etc. </div> </div> </div>Note that while he has a scientific and logical mind, to explain his spells, he knows that he is the one making them with the help of his Will. Is he a Scientist! or a Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T11:24:43-08:00","id":1349129,"title":"","content":"He\u2019s in really good shape, plus he\u2019s \u201cegoistic\u201d and \u201caggressive,\u201d so he probably either has a girlfriend or hooks up relatively often (assuming he has decent Social attributes)....<br /> <br /> Not being random here. You need to develop his social backstory as well as the physical and mental aspects.<br /> <br /> I think he sounds like more of a mage. He\u2019s basically a pulp hero, and pulp heroes are Etherites, not Technocrats. But it\u2019s your choice. Which paradigm (Science! or magick) most closely fits the kind of character you want to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T17:04:32-08:00","id":1349205,"title":"","content":"From what you've said I'd say he was more on the science side. There is a distinct manner in which he operates his awakened will, a strict way in which he connects with this energy source, and the inherent disposition to use science and his background in engineering. He wouldn't see it as mystical or as new-age mumbo jumbo (Im making assumptions here Ill admit) he sees it as science and therefore thats what it is. In his eyes all other mages both Tradition and Technocrat are simply using the same force but just not getting the idea of what it really is right. <br /> He's definitely very Etherite in sounding but then again Etherites are just Technocrat-lite with a dash of pseudoscience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T20:42:30-08:00","id":1349261,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a fairly typical Etherite, really. There's an example character in their first TradBook who has a similar &quot;New Thought&quot; methodology (the description notes that, in another life, they might have ended up in the Akashics.) This fits in more with the early Etherites (&quot;My character has One Big Theory&quot;) and less so with the radical methodological approach of Revised Etherites, but that's fine.<br /> <br /> &quot;Science&quot; is a dense word, and in Mage &quot;Will&quot; is, too, so I don't know that there's really going to be a tidy distinction to make. Is parapsychology more &quot;scientific&quot; than alchemy?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-17T21:01:13-08:00","id":1349266,"title":"","content":"I guess the question is, do you count Etherites as Science or magick (I always assumed magick because they were Tradition mages)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T05:10:03-08:00","id":1349311,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answers. <br /> <br /> The thing is, the char probably acknowledges himself as a mage. But he has a scientifical mind that explains magick. <br /> <br /> Regarding tradition, he would be a very different etherite or hermetic. Both traditions aren't known to use the instruments he uses.<br /> So, how would an etherite that sees himself as a mage and casting spells? Also, do Etherites believe in an enlightened Will that is making the effects? <br /> And how would a hermetic that see his spells with logical explanations and doesn't use symbolisms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-18-2019, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T11:28:53-08:00","id":1349384,"title":"","content":"The listed instruments are, again, pretty typical for a pulp hero Etherite. &quot;I have learned esoteric secrets, martial arts, and mesmerism in Tibet, and use these subtle arts and high-tech gadgets to fight crime.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Etherites do acknowledge a &quot;human factor&quot; (i.e. Will) as being a part of what's going on, it's just that their explanation tends to hew closer to what you propose for your character - there are psychic or spiritual energies which can change outcomes. I don't really run an edition that makes the distinction M20 does (between &quot;mystics&quot;, &quot;technomancers&quot; ,and &quot;technocrats&quot;) but in that system I guess I'd peg your dude as a technomancer - there are exotic forces which mages harness, and eventually they can activate them without an apparatus.<br /> <br /> What's a &quot;logical explanation&quot;? Hermetic magic seems very practical, it's just predicated on <i>phusikos</i> instead of physics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T16:19:45-08:00","id":1349465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349384#post1349384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The listed instruments are, again, pretty typical for a pulp hero Etherite. &quot;I have learned esoteric secrets, martial arts, and mesmerism in Tibet, and use these subtle arts and high-tech gadgets to fight crime.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Etherites do acknowledge a &quot;human factor&quot; (i.e. Will) as being a part of what's going on, it's just that their explanation tends to hew closer to what you propose for your character - there are psychic or spiritual energies which can change outcomes. I don't really run an edition that makes the distinction M20 does (between &quot;mystics&quot;, &quot;technomancers&quot; ,and &quot;technocrats&quot;) but in that system I guess I'd peg your dude as a technomancer - there are exotic forces which mages harness, and eventually they can activate them without an apparatus.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see. So, even that he <b>only</b> use those instruments, you don't think that's a problem for the Tradition? I mean, the char is not a genius at all, he doesn't have any PhD, he's a simple engineer that likes to have reasonable explanation for his effects. He also don't write papers or spend time in a lab. What you think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349384#post1349384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a &quot;logical explanation&quot;? Hermetic magic seems very practical, it's just predicated on <i>phusikos</i> instead of physics</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an explanation that isn't so simple as &quot;God did it&quot; or &quot;it works because that's the symbol of the sun&quot;, etc. He has a more detailed explanation, involving scientific concepts (like energy), but at the same time some kind of mysticism, because he acknowledges that it's him that's causing the effect with his Will.I thought an Etherite would not include the caster desire into the equation, things don't happen because you want them to happen, but because you made some thing to make it happen. For all they know, a machine could make it.<br /> <br /> I don't know what is phusikos... Also, how would a Hermetic that was taken from a scientific university would see the way Etherites do magick?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T17:16:37-08:00","id":1349468,"title":"","content":"Not every Etherite is a cloistered academic, and if someone has discovered an undocumented energy source capable of creating supernatural effects through meditation and eye contact, they're a genius, no matter the Int score on their character sheet. Etherites admit the possibility of psychic phenomena and undocumented energies with a subjective origin and manifestation, and New Thought is all about personal energy - again, nothing you've proposed has struck me as really out of the ordinary.<br /> <br /> I was being a little cute with &quot;phusikos&quot;, sorry. Hermetic sympathetic principles are part of natural magic, itself something of a precursor to modern science (the words &quot;physician&quot; and &quot;physics&quot; are both etymologically derived from the word for &quot;natural/physical&quot;.) It's an intricate system predicated on an internal logic, but it's paradigmatically (small P) different from its successors. Is that &quot;scientific&quot;? Or do you use &quot;scientific&quot; to mean &quot;using terms and stakes familiar to modern scientific discussion?&quot;<br /> <br /> A Hermetic who used to be a physicist sees the science they learned in college as a mere subset of the many important physical laws which govern the cosmos. If they have a rigid paradigm (see Guide to the Trads), they likely believe Etherites have stumbled on some (but not all) of these &quot;higher laws&quot;, and misunderstood or mislabeled them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-18T20:31:36-08:00","id":1349494,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Five Eyes;n1349468]Not every Etherite is a cloistered academic, and if someone has discovered an undocumented energy source capable of creating supernatural effects through meditation and eye contact, they're a genius, no matter the Int score on their character sheet. Etherites admit the possibility of psychic phenomena and undocumented energies with a subjective origin and manifestation, and New Thought is all about personal energy - again, nothing you've proposed has struck me as really out of the ordinary.{/quote]<br /> <br /> Indeed. The feel I have is that Etherite don't have the &quot;mage&quot; flavour. I feel that by playing an Etherite I'm not roleplaying a mage. That is because their Science! are too advanced in general. <br /> While the char do have a logical, &quot;scientifical&quot; explanation, I don't see him explaining his effects with all that crazy theories involving quantum-shit or &quot;ether spectrum&quot; babble. I feel that my char reasoning is too shallow. Maybe that's just my impression, or maybe I'm overthinking things.<br /> <br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Five Eyes;n1349468]I was being a little cute with &quot;phusikos&quot;, sorry. Hermetic sympathetic principles are part of natural magic, itself something of a precursor to modern science (the words &quot;physician&quot; and &quot;physics&quot; are both etymologically derived from the word for &quot;natural/physical&quot;.) It's an intricate system predicated on an internal logic, but it's paradigmatically (small P) different from its successors. Is that &quot;scientific&quot;? Or do you use &quot;scientific&quot; to mean &quot;using terms and stakes familiar to modern scientific discussion?&quot;<br /> <br /> What you mean by paradigmatically different from its successors? I use &quot;scientific&quot; to mean that it has an explanation that do not relly on mere symbolisms. And a practice that is based on basic scientific principles like: observating,formulating hypothesis, experimenting/testing, refining/eliminating based on the findings.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349468#post1349468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hermetic who used to be a physicist sees the science they learned in college as a mere subset of the many important physical laws which govern the cosmos. If they have a rigid paradigm (see Guide to the Trads), they likely believe Etherites have stumbled on some (but not all) of these &quot;higher laws&quot;, and misunderstood or mislabeled them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, to him, the Etherites are just tripping? Do you think he would have any use for his previous scientifical knowledge in his magick?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T00:14:10-08:00","id":1349511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349494#post1349494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use &quot;scientific&quot; to mean that it has an explanation that do not relly on mere symbolisms. And a practice that is based on basic scientific principles like: observating,formulating hypothesis, experimenting/testing, refining/eliminating based on the findings</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you - the Order of Hermes is very 'scientific' in the way they experiment with magick, study their findings, toss aside things that do not work, write down their reliable rituals and working symbols down in tomes by the libraryful, have a strict Mentor-Student relationship, and consider the concepts and structures behind what makes it all tick. There is a reason the Technocracy/Order Of Reason developed out of Hermes through the Freemasons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's also why House Tremere freaked out when their immortality rote started to fail - it was The True Way how to do it, that had been developed and studied over ages by them. Then they developed a new theory of how they could acquire immortality through the immortal blood of vampires and an adjustment to one of their rituals.<br /> The experiment failed. Very scientific<br /> <br /> Of all the Traditions, the Hermetics probably have the most structued 'scientific' approach to Magick.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T00:34:33-08:00","id":1349513,"title":"","content":"Fortunately, this is sort of <i>the </i>game for overthinking things. But on the whole I do think you've just described a fairly typical Etherite - they discover a force, they develop some terms to bracket it, they perform experiments to explore it... that's all by the book.<br /> <br /> Surely an undocumented cosmic force which responds to human mental energies and can do anything is kind of a &quot;big theory&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349494#post1349494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you mean by paradigmatically different from its successors?</div> </div> </div> </div>We would say that the effect of silver on a werewolf is &quot;supernatural&quot;, having no natural/physical explanation. You could break silver down into is components and none of them would contain the &quot;anti-werewolf&quot; part which reacts to werewolf bodies. Natural magic would say that silver's effect is &quot;natural&quot;, in that silver <i>by its nature </i>has an effect on werewolves.<br /> <br /> Or, to use a more grounded example, that water and ice are very different things, with different essential properties. This is an outgrowth of being the product of an intellectual tradition which has a wider category of &quot;physical existence&quot; than we use, and not having the same category of non-physicality which Enlightenment thinkers and their successors were using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349494#post1349494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use &quot;scientific&quot; to mean that it has an explanation that do not relly on mere symbolisms. And a practice that is based on basic scientific principles like: observating,formulating hypothesis, experimenting/testing, refining/eliminating based on the findings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think considering any well-explored explanation to be &quot;scientific&quot; is overbroad.<br /> <br /> &quot;Natural magic&quot; argues objects such as metals and plants have properties which can be harnessed to effect. Some of these are familiar and reducible to component properties - willow bark into aspirin, for instance. Some of these are more subtle, occult laws, which common folk aren't aware of. You can observe, document, and explore these properties. You can posit from past evidence whether or not something shares a property, by analogy in physical form or occult symbolism. You can test that position, and refine your understanding based on your findings.<br /> <br /> Yet I'd wager most people wouldn't call Verbena herbcraft or Hermetic protective amulets &quot;scientific&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349494#post1349494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, to him, the Etherites are just tripping? Do you think he would have any use for his previous scientifical knowledge in his magick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, anyone with a rigid paradigm is pretty sure everyone else has it wrong. And sure, that's part of why Flambeau recruits physicists and the Verbena recruit biologists - the mystic training they receive grows upon what they have already perceived, and gives it new meanings and properties. The Verbena don't think modern medicine <i>doesn't work, </i>they think there are forms of healing and types of illness normal biologists <i>aren't aware of.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T13:06:13-08:00","id":1349656,"title":"","content":"Just bringing back one subject, are you sure Etherites (in general, as a Tradition) acknowledge the power of the Will on their effects? I just took a look in the Trad book and couldn't find any hint about that. Only about using pshychic mind-power, which is not the same, nor practiced by any great number of Scientists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349513#post1349513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We would say that the effect of silver on a werewolf is &amp;quot;supernatural&amp;quot;, having no natural/physical explanation. You could break silver down into is components and none of them would contain the &amp;quot;anti-werewolf&amp;quot; part which reacts to werewolf bodies. Natural magic would say that silver's effect is &amp;quot;natural&amp;quot;, in that silver <i>by its nature </i>has an effect on werewolves.<br /> <br /> Or, to use a more grounded example, that water and ice are very different things, with different essential properties. This is an outgrowth of being the product of an intellectual tradition which has a wider category of &amp;quot;physical existence&amp;quot; than we use, and not having the same category of non-physicality which Enlightenment thinkers and their successors were using.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the werewolf thing, since that is not covered by regular science. But it is known that water snd ice have the same molecules, and a scientist (low case &quot;s&quot;) from any Tradition knows that. <br /> <br /> So, I'd say that an hermetic scientist only disagree with a sleeper science when it's about an uncovered subject. And that's when magick kicks in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think considering any well-explored explanation to be &amp;quot;scientific&amp;quot; is overbroad.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Natural magic&amp;quot; argues objects such as metals and plants have properties which can be harnessed to effect. Some of these are familiar and reducible to component properties - willow bark into aspirin, for instance. Some of these are more subtle, occult laws, which common folk aren't aware of. You can observe, document, and explore these properties. You can posit from past evidence whether or not something shares a property, by analogy in physical form or occult symbolism. You can test that position, and refine your understanding based on your findings.<br /> <br /> Yet I'd wager most people wouldn't call Verbena herbcraft or Hermetic protective amulets &amp;quot;scientific&amp;quot;. </div> </div> </div>Well, they surely sre using the scientific method. I would consider that they are at least trying to use science methods to explain/improve their beliefs.<br /> <br /> The thing is, Etherite Science is too much different from regular science. Etherite Science do not respect concepts like reproducibility, falsifiability or verifiability. So in a sense, their are less real life science than a mystic that separates magick from science.<br /> <br /> My char was an engineer, so he followed those principles I just posted. After awakening, he understood that there are somethings that can be done that do not follow those rules. This doesn't invalidate his previous knowledge, just like quantum physics do not invalidate relativity. Theu are just 2 separate things.<br /> So, as fsr as I understand, being an Etherite means that both low case and upper case &quot;s&quot; science must be mixed (and thus low case lost its meaning). While being an hermetic scientist means that magick is apart from science. Is that right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, anyone with a rigid paradigm is pretty sure everyone else has it wrong. And sure, that's part of why Flambeau recruits physicists and the Verbena recruit biologists - the mystic training they receive grows upon what they have already perceived, and gives it new meanings and properties. The Verbena don't think modern medicine <i>doesn't work, </i>they think there are forms of healing and types of illness normal biologists <i>aren't aware of.</i> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, if hermetic is chosen, definitely house flambeau was my thougth. Being an electrical engineer he deals a lot with electricity and have great knowledge about it. I wonder how this could affect his effects, maybe adding electromagnetism in his spells and explanations...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T14:48:16-08:00","id":1349692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349656#post1349656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just bringing back one subject, are you sure Etherites (in general, as a Tradition) acknowledge the power of the Will on their effects? I just took a look in the Trad book and couldn't find any hint about that. Only about using pshychic mind-power, which is not the same, nor practiced by any great number of Scientists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Define &quot;Will.&quot; Do Verbena believe in Will? Etherites consider personal genius/inspiration and the agonistic relationship with the external world to be essential in the process of Science. It's a necessarily subjective art - personal and internal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349656#post1349656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with the werewolf thing, since that is not covered by regular science. But it is known that water snd ice have the same molecules, and a scientist (low case &quot;s&quot;) from any Tradition knows that. So, I'd say that an hermetic scientist only disagree with a sleeper science when it's about an uncovered subject. And that's when magick kicks in.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're making a categorical distinction that a Hermetic or Verbena would not: between magical and natural law. To the view of natural magic (and by extension Hermetic philosophy), ice and water <i>aren't </i>the same. Their molecular properties aren't the full picture, and any Hermetic worth his pointy hat would know that Sleeper science is incomplete on the matter of, well, Matter.<br /> <br /> Proposing things like &quot;agreeing&quot; or &quot;disagreeing&quot; with &quot;science&quot; strikes me as a non-starter, especially if you can be &quot;scientific&quot; about things &quot;science&quot; doesn't &quot;agree&quot; with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349656#post1349656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, Etherite Science is too much different from regular science. Etherite Science do not respect concepts like reproducibility, falsifiability or verifiability. So in a sense, their are less real life science than a mystic that separates magick from science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Feyerabend would disagree, is rather the point - real-world science doesn't operate in the idealized fashion it is often described. In any case, Etherites do care about reproducibility by their peers and perform experiments to explore and dissect their theories (this process is, in fact, what they call Science.) They even do peer review (this is what Paradigma is for). They don't believe in reduction of entities or materialism, which are heuristic elements of science and not actual rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349656#post1349656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My char was an engineer, so he followed those principles I just posted. After awakening, he understood that there are somethings that can be done that do not follow those rules. This doesn't invalidate his previous knowledge, just like quantum physics do not invalidate relativity. Theu are just 2 separate things. So, as fsr as I understand, being an Etherite means that both low case and upper case &quot;s&quot; science must be mixed (and thus low case lost its meaning). While being an hermetic scientist means that magick is apart from science. Is that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sons of Ether believe all models to be incomplete and contingent by necessity. Models are descriptions of real things, but our ability to approach those real things is always mediated by subjectivity (until we Ascend). They believe Sleeper (and Technocratic) science is predicated on assuming one model is &quot;more correct&quot;, rejecting anything that doesn't fit. Etherite capital-Science tries to work in both directions - exploring models within themselves and also testing them with other, external models - not to invalidate them (which isn't really possible, because of how paradigms work) but rather to expand the knowledge base. This is discussed starting on Page 55 of their Revised Tradbook.<br /> <br /> In terms of your character, the Etherites don't consider their previous knowledge &quot;invalid&quot;, but it's not about a separate subject, either - there's no such thing as &quot;normal physics&quot; and &quot;magic physics&quot;, there's just &quot;physics&quot;, which is merely one (flawed, incomplete) way to try and explore and understand the real world. A studious Scientist would want to know (and experiment with) the &quot;physics&quot; explanation for how mental energy can direct Forces, but also would want to know (and experiment with) the &quot;martial arts qi gong&quot; explanation.<br /> <br /> The Hermetics believe in an order to the cosmos, which extends both to its physical contents and its spiritual ones. Things in the world have essential natures and various properties - some Sleeper science understands, some it does not. Magic is about harnessing these properties by various technical and spiritual methods.<br /> <br /> In terms of your character, a Flambeau electrical engineer knows both the basic physical laws which cause electricity to act like it does, and the higher mystical properties which govern <i>why </i>it has these traits. They know copper conducts, but also the occult <i>reason </i>why copper works as it does (its subtle properties.) The &quot;normal physics&quot; that Sleepers know about isn't a different <i>type </i>of knowledge, it's a subset of the actual rules which govern the universe - the surface knowledge. Knowing that stuff is &quot;practical&quot; but it's considered a stepping stone to the higher, spiritual lore (the &quot;theory&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T09:48:17-08:00","id":1349875,"title":"","content":"By any chance, are you familiar with the Scientific Mystic/Techgnosi Merit that's fine in <b>Book of Secrets</b>, p.45? This is exactly the sort of stuff that it deals with. It's a very common Merit among the Etherites (in fact, the Merit was first introduced in the Sons of Ether revised Tradition Book); but the only real requirement to having it is to be a practitioner of Weird Science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:11:02-08:00","id":1349878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349692#post1349692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Define &amp;quot;Will.&amp;quot; Do Verbena believe in Will? Etherites consider personal genius/inspiration and the agonistic relationship with the external world to be essential in the process of Science. It's a necessarily subjective art - personal and internal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta confess that I know little to nothing about Verbena focus and paradigms. But as I understand, the Hermetic *knows* that his Will is causing the change. The Etherites understand that a genius mind is necessary for creating/makingban effect, but they do not acknowledge it as one of the directs causes of the effect. For all they know, their presence isn't necessary for the devices to work, while the hermetic rituals require the mage specifically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're making a categorical distinction that a Hermetic or Verbena would not: between magical and natural law. To the view of natural magic (and by extension Hermetic philosophy), ice and water <i>aren't </i>the same. Their molecular properties aren't the full picture, and any Hermetic worth his pointy hat would know that Sleeper science is incomplete on the matter of, well, Matter. </div> </div> </div>Why they wouldn't? Being from scientific background, they can create a clear differentiation between what they learned in university and what they learned with their Tradition. <br /> But I agree with you, they know all the molecular properties of water/ice. I just wonder which other metaphysical property wouldn't be known by science.. Like..ice is colder and harder than water...? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Proposing things like &amp;quot;agreeing&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;disagreeing&amp;quot; with &amp;quot;science&amp;quot; strikes me as a non-starter, especially if you can be &amp;quot;scientific&amp;quot; about things &amp;quot;science&amp;quot; doesn't &amp;quot;agree&amp;quot; with. </div> </div> </div>Yes, as long as you apply scientific methods and reasoning, even in things averse to scientific principles, like magick, is enough for me.<br /> <br /> You kinda lost me here. Just to remember that your point is that Hermetic natural science is different from real life science. I believe that this is only true for mages that do not have a (real life) scientific paradigm. And that applies for Etherites as well. They might work with concepts completely different and unknown to RL science too. Or are you saying that *all* Hermetics work with that level of simbolism?<br /> <br /> To simplify, which science and methods you believe is closer to real life science: a Hermetic from engineering university or Etherite Science?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Feyerabend would disagree, is rather the point - real-world science doesn't operate in the idealized fashion it is often described. In any case, Etherites do care about reproducibility by their peers and perform experiments to explore and dissect their theories (this process is, in fact, what they call Science.) They even do peer review (this is what Paradigma is for). They don't believe in reduction of entities or materialism, which are heuristic elements of science and not actual rules. </div> </div> </div>I didn't know about Feyerabend, interesting ideas.<br /> <br /> Yes, but very often the effects cannot be reproduced and they still aren't discarded... Because it works!! Magick do not follow reproducibility - well, actually it does. Considering that you provide an Etherite with the same paradigm as the author too - so scientific principles cannot be applied to it, hence why it should be treated as a different thing than science. The same is true for falsifiability, Etherites do not discard a theory proved wrong...For the same reason os just said. <br /> The only way that a mage could really apply full real life scientific methods is if he understand that all paradigms are in fact just a support for a mage's Will and try to quantify and experiment considering all the &quot;rules&quot; we as players knows exists. But that's not gonna happen in game. However, I feel Hermerics were the ones that got closer by discovering the role of Will in magick and meta-gaming the Spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sons of Ether believe all models to be incomplete and contingent by necessity. Models are descriptions of real things, but our ability to approach those real things is always mediated by subjectivity (until we Ascend). They believe Sleeper (and Technocratic) science is predicated on assuming one model is &amp;quot;more correct&amp;quot;, rejecting anything that doesn't fit. Etherite capital-Science tries to work in both directions - exploring models within themselves and also testing them with other, external models - not to invalidate them (which isn't really possible, because of how paradigms work) but rather to expand the knowledge base. This is discussed starting on Page 55 of their Revised Tradbook.<br /> <br /> In terms of your character, the Etherites don't consider their previous knowledge &amp;quot;invalid&amp;quot;, but it's not about a separate subject, either - there's no such thing as &amp;quot;normal physics&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;magic physics&amp;quot;, there's just &amp;quot;physics&amp;quot;, which is merely one (flawed, incomplete) way to try and explore and understand the real world. A studious Scientist would want to know (and experiment with) the &amp;quot;physics&amp;quot; explanation for how mental energy can direct Forces, but also would want to know (and experiment with) the &amp;quot;martial arts qi gong&amp;quot; explanation.<br /> <br /> The Hermetics believe in an order to the cosmos, which extends both to its physical contents and its spiritual ones. Things in the world have essential natures and various properties - some Sleeper science understands, some it does not. Magic is about harnessing these properties by various technical and spiritual methods. </div> </div> </div>The thing is, magick and low case science to not behave in a ewual manner, so the Etherite shouldn't treat them as one. <br /> I understand that the Etherite try to mix them as being part of the same field of knowledge, while the Hermetics knows they are and behave differently (magick and sleeper science). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In terms of your character, a Flambeau electrical engineer knows both the basic physical laws which cause electricity to act like it does, and the higher mystical properties which govern <i>why </i>it has these traits. They know copper conducts, but also the occult <i>reason </i>why copper works as it does (its subtle properties.) The &amp;quot;normal physics&amp;quot; that Sleepers know about isn't a different <i>type </i>of knowledge, it's a subset of the actual rules which govern the universe - the surface knowledge. Knowing that stuff is &amp;quot;practical&amp;quot; but it's considered a stepping stone to the higher, spiritual lore (the &amp;quot;theory&amp;quot;.) </div> </div> </div>I understand. But wouldn't that be the view of a mahe with more mystical paradigms and High Ritual as practice? Do you believe a Hermetic with the focus I posted would have those beliefs as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T10:17:09-08:00","id":1349879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349875#post1349875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By any chance, are you familiar with the Scientific Mystic/Techgnosi Merit that's fine in <b>Book of Secrets</b>, p.45? This is exactly the sort of stuff that it deals with. It's a very common Merit among the Etherites (in fact, the Merit was first introduced in the Sons of Ether revised Tradition Book); but the only real requirement to having it is to be a practitioner of Weird Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am. But i find it quite unnecessary. And I am discussing about the view of the Traditions and the char, not only mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T14:16:32-08:00","id":1349915,"title":"","content":"If you do the Order of Herm\u00e8s thing, maybe consider House Tytalus? They also do a lot with Will, and Tytalus mages have more emotional discipline and self-control than Flambeau mages (typically).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T15:28:44-08:00","id":1349936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349878#post1349878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as I understand, the Hermetic *knows* that his Will is causing the change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm contending the &quot;human factor&quot; <i>is </i>Will, as <b>Mage </b>understands it. It's why I asked for your definition.<br /> <br /> The Etherites think Science can't happen without the person - it's a subjective art. (Their original Tradbook's synopsis of the Kitab just straight-up calls this faculty &quot;Will&quot;, in fact.)<br /> The Hemetics think the person is the most important part of magic - it's a personal art.<br /> <br /> What's the distinction?<br /> <br /> (Hermetic &quot;Will&quot; is a subset of the true Will, if this helps clarify things - they think &quot;Will&quot; is a narrower category than it really is.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349878#post1349878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why they wouldn't? Being from scientific background, they can create a clear differentiation between what they learned in university and what they learned with their Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, outside of simplification for the sake of brevity, would someone learn high school physics and graduate-level physics, and act like these were talking about different worlds?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349878#post1349878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To simplify, which science and methods you believe is closer to real life science: a Hermetic from engineering university or Etherite Science?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Etherites, hands down.<br /> <br /> Etherites are methodologically radical, but fundamentally practicing modern inquiry: experimentation, documentation, dissemination, peer review, reexamination. (And Feyerabend has done yeoman's work in talking about how this approach is actually <i>closer </i>to how real-world science is done than the ideal description, so it's not even that radical!)<br /> <br /> Natural magic (which Hermetic methods are modeled on) is a centuries-old paradigm (small-p) predicated on a pre-or-early-modern view of the composition of the physical and spiritual worlds.It's capable of ingesting and accommodating the engineer's knowledge, like any paradigm, but does so on its own terms, which is not the same thing as adopting another paradigm. (If this were not true, Technocrats believe in faeries.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349878#post1349878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so scientific principles cannot be applied to it, hence why it should be treated as a different thing than science.</div> </div> </div> </div>You yourself just defined the actual parameters of reproducibility of magic, though. Magick <i>can </i>be reproduced - that's what a Rote is. In fact, the Akashics and Euthanatos have fundamentally incompatible worldviews and paradigms (atman vs. anatman) and nevertheless have rotes pass back and forth.<br /> <br /> If an experiment only worked when the lab tech was Christian, could we nevertheless apply the scientific method?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349878#post1349878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same is true for falsifiability, Etherites do not discard a theory proved wrong...</div> </div> </div> </div>Etherites don't think a functional model <i>can </i>be usefully &quot;proven wrong,&quot; only proven incomplete. (We undergo this process in real-world science all the time, in fact - falsifiable positions and &quot;disproof&quot; are an <i>ideal </i>formed in an attempt to define &quot;science&quot;, but not all science does or even can make sense in light of that definition.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349878#post1349878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that the Etherite try to mix them as being part of the same field of knowledge, while the Hermetics knows they are and behave differently (magick and sleeper science).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite how I'd see it.<br /> <br /> <b>Ether </b>science holds Sleeper science to be an incomplete model among many other incomplete models. Capital-Science is about exploring and interrogating models to try and find the perspective and knowledge which will let you reconcile all of these models (which is Ascension.)<br /> <br /> <b>Technocratic </b>science holds Sleeper science to be the &quot;baby school&quot; version of the more complicated real physical laws which govern the cosmos. This is like the Etherites, in fact! But the Union holds its models to be the most accurate and correct, and thinks other models are inferior, both in being wrong about facts and in being irresponsible and dangerous ways to think.<br /> <br /> <b>Hermetic </b><i>scientia </i>holds Sleeper Science to be an immature understanding of the universe. It's not wrong or right, because it's only a part of the picture. It's good to have that knowledge, but by itself it's not enough to Awaken, much less Ascend. Quaesitori study music and mathematics because these things help them understand the higher, fundamental cosmic principles - they don't think &quot;music&quot; and &quot;magic&quot; are different, it's just that Sleepers don't see the hidden magic truth &quot;inside&quot; their music. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349878#post1349878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand. But wouldn't that be the view of a mahe with more mystical paradigms and High Ritual as practice? Do you believe a Hermetic with the focus I posted would have those beliefs as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be difficult to adopt Hermetic magic without accepting a Hermetic worldview and philosophy. Why would the character stay in a Tradition where they think the stuff all their peers and teachers believe in is irrational claptrap?<br /> <br /> In the context of this specific character, is &quot;being skeptical of received wisdom&quot; and &quot;experimenting with magic&quot; the key element? Those traits could fit into almost any Tradition.<br /> <br /> Is the important part &quot;translating magical terms into ones akin to Sleeper science&quot;? That's sort of a technomancer thing, especially Etherites.<br /> <br /> Is the important part &quot;buff and confrontational electrical engineer zaps chumps with kung fu&quot;? That's got a place in the Hermetics (Tytalus) and Akashics (Li Hai), among others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T04:11:44-08:00","id":1349997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the important part &quot;buff and confrontational electrical engineer zaps chumps with kung fu&quot;? That's got a place in the Hermetics (Tytalus) and Akashics (Li Hai), among others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth to mention Etherite Adventurers here: famous for combining esoteric brawl and practical engineering to survive their daring adventures...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T05:56:19-08:00","id":1350005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1349936#post1349936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm contending the &quot;human factor&quot; <i>is </i>Will, as <b>Mage </b>understands it. It's why I asked for your definition.<br /> <br /> The Etherites think Science can't happen without the person - it's a subjective art. (Their original Tradbook's synopsis of the Kitab just straight-up calls this faculty &quot;Will&quot;, in fact.)<br /> The Hemetics think the person is the most important part of magic - it's a personal art.<br /> <br /> What's the distinction?<br /> <br /> (Hermetic &quot;Will&quot; is a subset of the true Will, if this helps clarify things - they think &quot;Will&quot; is a narrower category than it really is.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I understand Will as true Will, the desire of the mage casting the effect. While the Etherites Will is in fact affecting the outcome (that's the truth in Mage), they do not hold it as part of the effect anymore than the guy that created a radio and turned it on. Of course, you have to understand the radio to make it play songs, give it to a chimp and it would play only statics. But it is not the Will of the Scientist that is making it play, it's the science behind the radio working.<br /> That's not how Hermetics view magick. You can't explain to someone how a wand works and that person will be able to cast spells. He needs to know what he is doing and have his true Will working on that.<br /> As I see, the Etherite can teach someone to operate the radio (only awakened minds could understand it), while the Hermetic must teach the student how to cast his Will on the effect.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why, outside of simplification for the sake of brevity, would someone learn high school physics and graduate-level physics, and act like these were talking about different worlds? </div> </div> </div>Because they are very, very different and don't share some basics principles of operation. Take my example of Quantum Mechanics and Relativity. But you made a good point, this also happens in some real life subjects. I guess it would vary from mage to mage and their paradgim. How different are his sleeper paradigm and after his awake.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Etherites, hands down.<br /> <br /> Etherites are methodologically radical, but fundamentally practicing modern inquiry: experimentation, documentation, dissemination, peer review, reexamination. (And Feyerabend has done yeoman's work in talking about how this approach is actually <i>closer </i>to how real-world science is done than the ideal description, so it's not even that radical!)<br /> <br /> Natural magic (which Hermetic methods are modeled on) is a centuries-old paradigm (small-p) predicated on a pre-or-early-modern view of the composition of the physical and spiritual worlds.It's capable of ingesting and accommodating the engineer's knowledge, like any paradigm, but does so on its own terms, which is not the same thing as adopting another paradigm. (If this were not true, Technocrats believe in faeries.) </div> </div> </div>You are comparing Etherites modern Science with natural philosophy, like the ancient greece one. That's not what I'm talking about. I'm talking about a Hermetic with a good real life scientific knowledge and beliefs that awakened and started studying the occult and applying scientific principles on it, whenever possible. It's more about the engineering knowledge acomodating the esoteric one than the other way around.<br /> <br /> My point is that this guy is more &quot;scientific&quot; than the average Etherite, that rolls on top of real life science principles like a train.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You yourself just defined the actual parameters of reproducibility of magic, though. Magick <i>can </i>be reproduced - that's what a Rote is. In fact, the Akashics and Euthanatos have fundamentally incompatible worldviews and paradigms (atman vs. anatman) and nevertheless have rotes pass back and forth.<br /> <br /> If an experiment only worked when the lab tech was Christian, could we nevertheless apply the scientific method? </div> </div> </div>Yes, if determine that one of the initial conditions of working is the lab tech being Christian. And it will work in this condition. The problem with magick is that the mages do not really knows why it works, they all have their different paradigms, but in the end of the day it works because of the mage\u2019s Will.<br /> That\u2019s why it is easier for the ones that believe in Will to be more scientific and to accept others paradigms (\u201cHis prayers only works because he\u2019s focusing his will through them\u201d).<br /> That\u2019s why Etherites can\u2019t effectively disprove a theory (it is right,for some Scientist) and why they are fighting all the time.<br /> Also, a rote is not reproducing the same experiment, is obtaining the same result. Akashic and Euthanatos adapt their techniques to achieve the same thing. Hermetics do that all the time with their spells, that's why they are efficient in their spellcasting and their view on magick.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not quite how I'd see it.<br /> <br /> <b>Ether </b>science holds Sleeper science to be an incomplete model among many other incomplete models. Capital-Science is about exploring and interrogating models to try and find the perspective and knowledge which will let you reconcile all of these models (which is Ascension.)<br /> <br /> <b>Technocratic </b>science holds Sleeper science to be the &quot;baby school&quot; version of the more complicated real physical laws which govern the cosmos. This is like the Etherites, in fact! But the Union holds its models to be the most accurate and correct, and thinks other models are inferior, both in being wrong about facts and in being irresponsible and dangerous ways to think.<br /> <br /> <b>Hermetic </b><i>scientia </i>holds Sleeper Science to be an immature understanding of the universe. It's not wrong or right, because it's only a part of the picture. It's good to have that knowledge, but by itself it's not enough to Awaken, much less Ascend. Quaesitori study music and mathematics because these things help them understand the higher, fundamental cosmic principles - they don't think &quot;music&quot; and &quot;magic&quot; are different, it's just that Sleepers don't see the hidden magic truth &quot;inside&quot; their music. </div> </div> </div>Very good descriptions. I am curious to know where did you took this \u201cscientia\u201d from. Maybe it\u2019s from real world hermeticism? Because in Mage, it seems the core of Hermetic paradigm is the true Will. Everything derive from it and are mere tools for focusing it. So, things like the four (or five) elements, astrology, symbolism, etc. are taugth as ways to direct that Will and might not be practiced by every Hermetic. I think those are subjects of practitioners of High Ritual Magick and Alchemy only.<br /> Your Quaesitori knows that music, mathematics and magick are different thing. But they are related in a sense that he uses both music and mathematic to cast magick.<br /> Maybe I\u00b4m not getting your point here...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it would be difficult to adopt Hermetic magic without accepting a Hermetic worldview and philosophy. Why would the character stay in a Tradition where they think the stuff all their peers and teachers believe in is irrational claptrap? </div> </div> </div>And what would be the Hermetic world view and philosophy? <br /> As I said, I think there isn\u2019t a Hermetic fixed worldview except that you are creating spells with your Will. Not all Hermetics believe in symbols, or in angels/demons or in zodiac. What they seem to share is the notion that those focus help in casting their Will.<br /> And the Tradition as a whole seem to give credit to intelligent, dedicated and power/knowledge hungry people. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the context of this specific character, is &quot;being skeptical of received wisdom&quot; and &quot;experimenting with magic&quot; the key element? Those traits could fit into almost any Tradition.<br /> Is the important part &quot;translating magical terms into ones akin to Sleeper science&quot;? That's sort of a technomancer thing, especially Etherites.<br /> Is the important part &quot;buff and confrontational electrical engineer zaps chumps with kung fu&quot;? That's got a place in the Hermetics (Tytalus) and Akashics (Li Hai), among others. </div> </div> </div>The char thing is something like: He\u2019s na engineer and understands how the universe works. Then he awakes and sees that there are more out there than we know. He knows that it is something related with his Will and counsciousness. He tries to deal with it the more scientifically possible, without any metaphors nor faith nor symbolism. He also can\u2019t blend it with sleeper science per se, that quantum mechanics bullshit or waves spectrum. He understands all of that from his engineer knowledge and knows that magick is not this. He just tries to apply scientific principles in his magick and tries to study it.<br /> I\u2019d say your first example is the closer one. So, he definitely could fit both Traditions.<br /> It would be very good to know how those Hermetics that come from physics or scientific places adapt to Hermetic philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T07:21:00-08:00","id":1350008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350005#post1350005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Quaesitori knows that music, mathematics and magick are different thing. But they are related in a sense that he uses both music and mathematic to cast magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Quaesitor example in the Tradition Book that's a musician and mathematician begs to differ...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OoH Trad Book p.97</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...the Masters had been striving for enlightenement trough art. Composers like Beethoven and Bach were students of esoteric spirituality, <b>c</b>apturing sublime essence in waves of sound...as you studied these Masters -their lives, vision and works -the world itself began to sing<br /> <br /> ...spun from Pythagorean accords on a variety of instruments, this <i>Symphony Hermetica</i> caught the ear...of a Quaesitor<br /> <br /> ...your music contains a profound element of order. Orchestrated to inspire harmonic clarity, these compositions affect people on levels few of them trully understand...<br /> <br /> ...To you <b>music is a sacred art</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Music and symbolism seem to be<i> pretty magical</i> to him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-21-2019, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T11:56:02-08:00","id":1350079,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> I Liked your post (I forgot about the Adventurers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T14:01:09-08:00","id":1350115,"title":"","content":"It's gonna take some convincing to make me buy the argument that Hermetics don't think True Names and Angelic Seals have real power. Even House Ex Misc funnels its stuff through the principles of Hermetic high ritual (see their section in the Rev TradBook.) They use novel symbols and forge new divine shapes to resonate with, but they're still operating in a Hermetic (natural) paradigm. (In this analogy, natural magic is the car, occult principles are the keys, and Will is the engine. It's essential to do anything, but the other parts are just as important. Wands are a device to help you find your keys. It's the <i>Akashics </i>who think mystic signs have no inherent power on their own, only serving to focus the will - see their TradBook.)<br /> <br /> Hermetics don't think other Traditions are really exercising Will (See their old Tradbook, pg 58. This is also hinted at on Pg 62 of the Red Tradbook) If Hermetic &quot;Will&quot; was the same thing as <b>Mage </b>Will, only Hermetic characters would be mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350005#post1350005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that this guy is more &quot;scientific&quot; than the average Etherite, that rolls on top of real life science principles like a train.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's more materialistic and single-model focused, but single-theory-guy is still among the stock Etherites. I think framing it as &quot;accommodating esoteric principles into engineering ones&quot; really aims at a technomancer - in your character's case, probably an Etherite with a psionics or parapsychology model (&quot;there are untapped mental energies the brain can tap into, which can create supernatural effects.&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350005#post1350005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious to know where did you took this \u201cscientia\u201d from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their TradBooks describe their practice and how one harnesses occult principles and commands the gods. Even the most abstruse form of internalized magic, <i>magia, </i>is described in terms of occult principles (realizing potent archetypes internally as part of &quot;As above so below&quot;.) The instruments ultimately aren't necessary to harness these forces, but that's not because the occult forces aren't real and powerful - it's because the mage can realize their essential qualities without needing physical props.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T18:19:39-08:00","id":1350161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350115#post1350115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's gonna take some convincing to make me buy the argument that Hermetics don't think True Names and Angelic Seals have real power. Even House Ex Misc funnels its stuff through the principles of Hermetic high ritual (see their section in the Rev TradBook.) They use novel symbols and forge new divine shapes to resonate with, but they're still operating in a Hermetic (natural) paradigm. (In this analogy, natural magic is the car, occult principles are the keys, and Will is the engine. It's essential to do anything, but the other parts are just as important. Wands are a device to help you find your keys. It's the <i>Akashics </i>who think mystic signs have no inherent power on their own, only serving to focus the will - see their TradBook.)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some beliefs that all Hermetics share, some that most Hermetics share and some that are very individual particular. I'd say that The fact that magick is a result of your Will being manifested is common to all Hermetics. Maybe True Names are used by most of them. And there are lots of things that each individual believe that makes them different. It's the case of tha Quaesitor example you gave about music. It's something that isn't part of Hermetic philosophy, but it isn't wrong or bad believing. As long as the mage share <i>some</i> belief, specially the more fundamental ones, it's ok.<br /> <br /> Again, your examples of four elements, astrology, angelic seals are part of two practices: High Ritual and Alchemy. While those are very common practices, they aren't a requisite. We have plety of examples in Trad book that do not have them, being the Quaesitor one of them. His spells comes from his music and do not involve any of those aspects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hermetics don't think other Traditions are really exercising Will (See their old Tradbook, pg 58. This is also hinted at on Pg 62 of the Red Tradbook) If Hermetic &quot;Will&quot; was the same thing as <b>Mage </b>Will, only Hermetic characters would be mages. </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are. Hermetic Will is the same as Mage Will and all mages are using their Will to cast spells, except that they (majority) do not know that. The Hermetics very explanation of why other mage's spells work is because they are using their Will without even knowing. Also, I`m not familiar with old editions, we should stick with M20, please. Maybe Rev too, but remember that Rev had very different focus rules...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He's more materialistic and single-model focused, but single-theory-guy is still among the stock Etherites. I think framing it as &quot;accommodating esoteric principles into engineering ones&quot; really aims at a technomancer - in your character's case, probably an Etherite with a psionics or parapsychology model (&quot;there are untapped mental energies the brain can tap into, which can create supernatural effects.&quot;) </div> </div> </div>Yes, definitely. I know my char can fit easily in both Traditions, with both paradigms. I just have to decide which one.<br /> <br /> My issue with the Etherite Adventurer is that I would pretty much want a &quot;mage&quot; flavour to the character. An intelligent, scientific mage. While the Etherite seems to shout &quot;scientist&quot;. That's why I asked if Etherites saw themselves as mages before. Also, he won`t be publishing any papers and will probably not interact so much inside the Tradition due to his rigid paradigm...<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Hermetics are &quot;mages&quot; flavoured and, of the mystic Traditions, is the most scientific based, having structured the Sphere system and studying the working of magick.However, I have yet to think how a heavily scientific based mind would go inside the Tradition. I know they are very welcomed and there are examples of people like this, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their TradBooks describe their practice and how one harnesses occult principles and commands the gods. Even the most abstruse form of internalized magic, <i>magia, </i>is described in terms of occult principles (realizing potent archetypes internally as part of &quot;As above so below&quot;.) The instruments ultimately aren't necessary to harness these forces, but that's not because the occult forces aren't real and powerful - it's because the mage can realize their essential qualities without needing physical props. </div> </div> </div>Yes &quot;As above, so bellow&quot; is a fundamental element of Hermeticism that probably would fit my char, as counsiousness and reality could work as the &quot;above&quot; and &quot;bellow&quot;. The drop of instruments is explained in M20 as the Mage realising that its his Will doing the work, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T18:22:10-08:00","id":1350163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350008#post1350008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the Quaesitor example in the Tradition Book that's a musician and mathematician begs to differ...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Music and symbolism seem to be<i> pretty magical</i> to him...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think he do not. His music is a focus of his Art, this is quite clear. He considers it a sacred art, not the same as <b>The </b>Art. He can play music and do nothing with magick. They are not the same thing. They are related, though. Also, I think this one does not use mathematics, even though Pytagoras is briefly cited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-21T18:54:18-08:00","id":1350166,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Music of the Spheres&quot; is about occult correspondences - it's musical astrology. It's hardly a &quot;non-ritual&quot; practice. And it's unsurprisingly based on maths.<br /> <br /> Even just with recourse to M20's core, you can see the importance of these core concepts to Hermetics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20 Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemy, dominion, and High Ritual form core practices within the Order\u2019s ranks.<br /> No Hermetic mage lacks such training.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other practices are <i>added </i>to this foundation, but it's the heart of the <i>Ars</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350161#post1350161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, they are. Hermetic Will is the same as Mage Will and all mages are using their Will to cast spells, except that they (majority) do not know that. The Hermetics very explanation of why other mage's spells work is because they are using their Will without even knowing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they? Their original Tradbook specifically contradicts this, and the attitude holds in Revised and their M20 entry - other mages are ignorant, unfocused, and servile, not Willful. Do you think a Hermetic believes you can exercise Will by <i>begging</i>?<br /> <br /> In the older material, <i>magia</i>, working magic through the self/personal Will, is the highest of the three magical arts - one which Hermetics think only the Akashics brush up against. They consider every Dreamspeaker and Technocrat to be wallowing in the same tier of magic as the basest apprentice, <i>goetia</i>. This hierarchical view is echoed in their M20 entry, where &quot;even the Akashics&quot; are again given separate consideration.<br /> <br /> Unsurprisingly, as Brucato worked on the old Tradbook's appendix, where this material is from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T05:46:47-08:00","id":1350211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350163#post1350163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he do not. His music is a focus of his Art, this is quite clear. He considers it a sacred art, not the same as <b>The </b>Art. He can play music and do nothing with magick. They are not the same thing. They are related, though. Also, I think this one does not use mathematics, even though Pytagoras is briefly cited.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a trivial relation, though, but a necessary one. The Music of Spheres IS what he learned at his Awakening (ergo, magick), that's literally what he says. He can refuse to use the &quot;Music of the Spheres&quot; to create effects, but all the magick he does exists within that &quot;paradigmatical frame&quot;. Hence, the magick comes from music even if not all music it's magick<br /> <br /> More so, he thinks the world it's a worse place because people like pop and rock and ignore the work of &quot;the masters&quot;. He thinks that Beethoven has occult symbolism that can Awaken people...indicating that, in a way, he *can't* &quot;play music and do nothing with magick&quot;. Music changes the world in supernatural ways even without the Spheres being explicitly called out, or at least that's what he seems to believe. <hr />As <i>Seven Eyes</i> indicates, the OoH (all editions) dedicate a non trivial amount of pages to *qualify* Hermetic beliefs, and their definition of &quot;Will&quot; as more than merely &quot;Desire -&gt; Magick&quot;.<br /> <br /> Obviously M20, lacking space, can't qualify Will as much as the Trad books...that shouldn't be basis to say the fluff was retconned. You mention that Focus has changed, but the way it has changed only places more emphasis on the idea that Focus it's a necessary element of magick: previous editions also allowed to surpass instruments, but hadn't a language indicating explicitly that Practice/Paradigm it's never surpassed. Hence, Mages *do* believe that their Paradigm/Practice it's the way magick works (That's the definition of Paradigm in M20). Nothing of these mechanics disprove or retcon anything that was said about Will in previous books, as far as I can see. If anything, it makes the nature of *Will* (and how it may or may not diverge from the Purple) all the more important for Hermetics<br /> <br /> Now, there are some Hermetics that get closer to your definition of &quot;Will&quot;: Those that practice Chaos Magick rather than Ritual Magick DO think that purpose and desire (properly focused. Usually through symbols that are meaningful for the practitioner) it's all that matters, but they are an outlier. More often than not, Hermetics are shown as a very traditional Tradition, masters of High Ritual, and scoffing at these &quot;new agers&quot;<br /> <br /> Because Mage's Magic(k) it's loosely based arround Crowley teachings, that Pradigm it's actually &quot;true&quot; to the rules (to some extent)...but that has nothing to do with chaos magicians being known for applying the &quot;scientific method&quot; to magick... <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My issue with the Etherite Adventurer is that I would pretty much want a &quot;mage&quot; flavour to the character. </div> </div> </div>I think that's a<i> very good reason</i> to want to play Hermetic. One that trumps everything else, in fact....however, what's a &quot;mage&quot; flavor?<br /> <br /> When I think *mages*, I see Rituals, Pointy Hats, Wands. The reason why every time you bring this subject (as you've done several times, if my memory doesn't fail) people keeps shoving Etherites at you it's because he doesn't *feel* like a magician.<br /> <br /> I think you need a little more wizardry embbeded in your Character's Traits, if you want people to be convinced he's not just practicing a form of Weird Science (perhaps with mystical elements, but still mostly Science!). Dr Strange, after all, dresses the part...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-22-2019, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T07:22:12-08:00","id":1350221,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a>, yes, those are their foundations. Do that means that <b>no</b> hermetic exists without that practices? While M20 says so, rev and trad books put more focus on Will than specifics practices. Afterall, not all Hermetics go through all the training frombthe beginning, a mage can awake, learn about magick and join the Tradition later. Also, we have the example of the Olympian in trad book that uses his body as a focus. I know it is loosely explained and have room to shove alchemy or HR in his concept, but nevertheless he isn't the usual Hermetic.<br /> <br /> About their view on others, I thougth that mages always found some way to fit their own paradigm into others practices : the etherite do not believe the chorister's spells are miracles of god, he is in truth ressonating his prayers and singing into the right frequency to achieve what he wants. The same way, the Hermetic believes it's the Verbena Will, not his blood sacrifice that is changing reality. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350211#post1350211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously M20, lacking space, can't qualify Will as much as the Trad books...</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand, all mages chsnge reality through their Will, the only difference is that Hermetics knows that and put emphasis on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, there are some Hermetics that get closer to your definition of &amp;quot;Will&amp;quot;: Those that practice Chaos Magick rather than Ritual Magick DO think that purpose and desire (properly focused. Usually through symbols that are meaningful for the practitioner) it's all that matters, but they are an outlier. More often than not, Hermetics are shown as a very traditional Tradition, masters of High Ritual, and scoffing at these &amp;quot;new agers&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Because Mage's Magic(k) it's loosely based arround Crowley teachings, that Pradigm it's actually &amp;quot;true&amp;quot; to the rules (to some extent)...but that has nothing to do with chaos magicians being known for applying the &amp;quot;scientific method&amp;quot; to magick... <hr /> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I know that the char would not be the standard Hermetic (nor Etherite). I also know that Chaos Magick has nothing to do with science. As I said, I want a &quot;mage&quot; touch in him. Just not so much to use symbolism or pure faith, afterall he is an engineer. I also don't want him to be a Scientist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that's a<i> very good reason</i> to want to play Hermetic. One that trumps everything else, in fact....however, what's a &amp;quot;mage&amp;quot; flavor?<br /> <br /> When I think *mages*, I see Rituals, Pointy Hats, Wands. The reason why every time you bring this subject (as you've done several times, if my memory doesn't fail) people keeps shoving Etherites at you it's because he doesn't *feel* like a magician.<br /> <br /> I think you need a little more wizardry embbeded in your Character's Traits, if you want people to be convinced he's not just practicing a form of Weird Science (perhaps with mystical elements, but still mostly Science!). Dr Strange, after all, dresses the part... </div> </div> </div>To me, a mage is someone that cast spells, that works with energies or things that are arcane, unknown. Doesn't mean you can't be skeptical while working with it and try to understand its workings. He is a mage because he uses his very own counsciousness and Will to change reality in very wondrous ways.<br /> A Scientist (upper case) is someone who do not see anything &quot;special&quot; in what he's doing. It's all part of nature and he will always have a complete understanding and explanation (often too trippy) for what he's doing. Correct me if I'm wrong, but would an Etherite see himself casting a spell?<br /> <br /> Now, I don't want him to be a Scientist, because I don't want him to explain his effects using highly advanced scientific explanations. He won't explain telekinesis with complex quantum stuff. He knows quantum physics and that is not what he's doing. <br /> He is a scientist (low case) in a sense that he is rational, tries to understand the functioning of things and is skeptical (as far as possible). He do not work with pure faith (&quot;God did it&quot;) nor symbolisms, he believes that those who do can do it because of their own beliefs and are just focusing their Will.<br /> <br /> You don't need high ritual or pointy hats to be a mage. Wouldn't you consider akashic mages, then??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T07:58:18-08:00","id":1350234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350221#post1350221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand, all mages chsnge reality through their Will, the only difference is that Hermetics knows that and put emphasis on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But even the Hermetics don't believe that Magick itself simply consists of awakened Will taking shape - to them, Magick is a combination of their will, and the literal Magickal powers they see inherent in their tools and symbols.<br /> <br /> It's like the reverse of the Purple Paradigm, actually. Hermetics don't use the symbols and tools to steer their Will into reality - it's the opposite way around. They use their will to direct the external powers inherent in the Rituals, symbols, Names and what-have-you to get what they want. It is very much the dominion of the Hermetic's will over external sources of Magick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T11:29:51-08:00","id":1350270,"title":"","content":"That's my opinion too.<br /> <br /> I'm going to divide my answer in two sections:<br /> <br /> 1) Dispelling misconceptions about Etherites<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I don't want him to be a Scientist, because I don't want him to explain his effects using highly advanced scientific explanations. He won't explain telekinesis with complex quantum stuff. He knows quantum physics and that is not what he's doing.<br /> He is a scientist (low case) in a sense that he is rational, tries to understand the functioning of things and is skeptical (as far as possible). He do not work with pure faith (&quot;God did it&quot;) nor symbolisms, he believes that those who do can do it because of their own beliefs and are just focusing their Will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing of this precludes being a Scientist. Theories don't need to be particularly advanced (what's advanced physics about using &quot;alien crystals to power psionic rays&quot;?), wanting to understand ancient magic using the scientific method can easily be the focus of Science!, as Five Eyes explained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Scientist (upper case) is someone who do not see anything &quot;special&quot; in what he's doing. It's all part of nature and he will always have a complete understanding and explanation (often too trippy) for what he's doing. </div> </div> </div>Now, that's just wrong. To say that Science! it's part of &quot;nature&quot; it's as tivial as to say that this forum it's part of reality. OF course it's part of &quot;nature&quot; as long as &quot;nature&quot; means &quot;the universe&quot;/&quot;Reality(tm)&quot;/&quot;everything that exist&quot;.<br /> <br /> If &quot;nature&quot; means anything else, then Science! goes clearly above and beyond it by positing that reality extends far beyond that poorly understood &quot;nature&quot;. That's what the Wall of Troy represents, it's the limit of understanding.<br /> <br /> What small s scientists believe it's &quot;nature&quot; it's just a small subset of nature understood as the capital R, Reality(tm). Science! doesn't care much about what scientists say simply because it's users have discovered that there's so much more in the universe. It can be argued that Scientists! will never have a complete understanding until they can pull all of the universe inside the Wall of Troy. That (if possible), would be Ascencion.<br /> <br /> But even if they do have a pet theory that explains everything they do (that was more common in 2nd ed than nowdays, as Five Eyes said), that's not to say that they believe what they do can be explained within the framework of current science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correct me if I'm wrong, but would an Etherite see himself casting a spell? </div> </div> </div>Now, that's more polemical. And I will elaborate on this latter<br /> <br /> 2)My actual point it's aesthetical (but should also have a mechanic)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350221#post1350221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't need high ritual or pointy hats to be a mage. Wouldn't you consider akashic mages, then??</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in that sense, at least not in general.<br /> <br /> In fact, when I first opened Mage 2e back in the day (had already played Vampire and Ars Magica) I was pretty shocked: My opinion was <b>&quot;this isn't a game about mages!, this it's a game about hippies with reality warping superpowers &quot;</b>. <br /> <br /> My oppinion changed with time, and knowing RL mages...but that doesn't change that the aesthetics of Mage are fundamentally different from the pop-culture vision of what a wizard is (a vision very influenced by Tolkien, Conan, D&amp;D...). Akashicks are more &quot;magely&quot; than the Etherites, but they're still far from the stereotype. Most are based on the crazy kung-fu troope. As a D&amp;D nerd: Akashicks are clearly Monks (or Tome of Battle &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;casters&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; if you want to push it).<br /> <br /> Hermetics (and Verbena) are <b>aesthetically </b>the closest to being wizardly wizards. Even the intelectual outlook of the Hermetics it's very D&amp;D wizard themed (unsurprising, since they come from Ars Magica, and Ars had as one of it's goals to remake the &quot;old timer&quot; D&amp;D image of wizards w/o arbitrary limitations like being unable to cast in armor).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, a mage is someone that cast spells, that works with energies or things that are arcane, unknown. Doesn't mean you can't be skeptical while working with it and try to understand its workings. He is a mage because he uses his very own counsciousness and Will to change reality in very wondrous ways. </div> </div> </div>What you've just said it's empty of <b>aesthetic</b>. It's formless and thus says nothing about your character:<br /> <br /> &quot;he uses his very own counsciousness and Will to change reality&quot;.<br /> Everyone does that, literally means nothing.<br /> <br /> &quot;To me, a mage is someone that cast spells, that works with energies or things that are arcane, unknown. &quot;<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Now, that may be of interest: But what IS this &quot;casting spells&quot; you're talking about? .</span><br /> <br /> An Etherite won't be caught dead chanting an enochian incantation w/o some theory about why that works...<b>but</b><b>, as described,</b><b> neither will your character.</b> You stated, very clearly, that <i>your character doesn't place any value on those &quot;Instruments&quot;</i>, <i>they aren't MAGICAL!</i>. They are merely<i> a tool to chanel your mental power in order to weave the <b>&quot;totally not ether&quot; </b>field into phenomena</i>.<br /> <br /> And that's what an Etherite would say (except he would be manipulating the &quot;ether field&quot; rather than the &quot;not ether field&quot;)<br /> <br /> If you want to *call* this magic, well, that makes you a Scientific Mystic (that's what the Feat it's for)<br /> <br /> Mystics, even Chaos Magicians, think their magical spells are magical. Chaos Magicians believe that the power of their symbols comes from the fact that these matter to them and to others. They have power because they are a placeholder of the Will manifested trough their own lives and those of the people that surrounds them (hence why Chaos Mages use pop culture symbols so much, they are already *charged* with magick in their worldview because they matter to a lot of people). As simplified as Chaos Magick it's, it still places more importance on the symbols as placeholders of the Will than your mage that uses them as a mere way to focus that <s>psionic power</s> Will, and denies them any sort of magick outside of his use.<br /> <br /> If you want to sell me a Chaos Magician, <i>aesthetically</i>, there needs to be less emphasis on the pseudo-scientific theories about why magick stuff *really* works and more emphasis on the <b>arcane/esoteric/mystical </b>side of how magick stuff *really* works .<br /> That's not to say you can't <i>reason </i>why these work and try to apply the scientific method, it's just that these &quot;mystical spells&quot; need to be more the focus of the character and less of a meaningless word to declare an Effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-22-2019, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T14:04:33-08:00","id":1350306,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that no Hermetic gets out of their apprenticeship without learning the core of the Hermetic style, as learning the three types of magic &quot;in proper order&quot; is seen as important. As the RevTradBook notes that even Ex Misc, where all the weirdos are, funnels <i>everyone </i>through the high ritual practice, I see no reason to think the example Tytalus athlete is somehow not using the usual Hermetic instruments and practices. This accords with the style described in the prior material and in the Rev corebook, and with M20's entry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Scientist (upper case) is someone who do not see anything &quot;special&quot; in what he's doing. It's all part of nature and he will always have a complete understanding and explanation (often too trippy) for what he's doing. </div> </div> </div>Hermetics think magic is part of nature, too - every spell is the consequence of occult laws of sympathy, resonance, and essence. This is sort of where I've been stumbling - high ritual isn't superstitious or faith-based. It's very practical and rigorous. The planet Mercury, quartz crystals, and the color red have certain properties. Through Will, you harness them. Even linear sorcerers, with no mastery of their Will, can manage this - wands actually do stuff. (If they didn't, there would be no reason to keep dangerous occult secrets <i>secret</i>.) Remember, the Hermetic description isn't &quot;the gods are mere notions which let me focus my Will.&quot; Rather, it's &quot;with sufficient Will, I will order the gods to act, and they will do as I say.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Even chaos magicians don't think their created divine archetypes and the thoughtforms they make use of are trivial - once created or accepted, they're as real as any god, and can make the same demands. Morrison's got a whole thing about the spiritual struggle to uproot an archetype which has grown cancerous, and it's just as hard as trying to &quot;kill&quot; an evil god.)<br /> <br /> How does your character differentiate an &quot;energy&quot; which responds to &quot;consciousness and desire&quot;, and Etherites claiming &quot;psychic power&quot; can alter the physical world? Like, how would this character describe how he can create or direct electricity with &quot;desire&quot;? Is he saying this &quot;energy field&quot; can generate some undocumented force which leaves his brain and then goes to influence the movement of electrical charge? By what mechanism? How is adding entities to the scientific corpus in this way any different than what an Etherite does?<br /> <br /> Is the goal some sort of &quot;mystic&quot; character who has no &quot;mystical&quot; beliefs? Or just no beliefs they can't articulate in language which would look acceptably &quot;scientific&quot; to a normal Sleeper?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T14:35:02-08:00","id":1350312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350270#post1350270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's my opinion too.<br /> <br /> I'm going to divide my answer in two sections:<br /> <br /> 1) Dispelling misconceptions about Etherites<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nothing of this precludes being a Scientist. Theories don't need to be particularly advanced (what's advanced physics about using &quot;alien crystals to power psionic rays&quot;?), wanting to understand ancient magic using the scientific method can easily be the focus of Science!, as Five Eyes explained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they do! Even simple, obvious and old theories like Newton's Gravitational Force has some degree of complexity in its explanation and mathematics equations. Something as incredible as telekinesis surely will be very complex to study and understand.<br /> Of course that I, as a player, do not have to bring complex explanations or equations, but the character as a Scientist would. Unless he's a shitty Scientist..or a mage. <br /> <br /> Imagine he's first presenting to the Etherites:<br /> <br /> - Ok, you say you are able to create fire just by the use of your mind, how does it works?<br /> -I don't know, I just know it is related to my counsciousness being one with Reality and capable of shapping it.<br /> -Nonsene! Are you using you cerebral waves to vibrate quantum particles in a high frequency to make the comburent catch fire?<br /> -Dude, I'm just focusing my Will into th..<br /> -Get the fuck outta my face!!!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, that's just wrong. To say that Science! it's part of &quot;nature&quot; it's as tivial as to say that this forum it's part of reality. OF course it's part of &quot;nature&quot; as long as &quot;nature&quot; means &quot;the universe&quot;/&quot;Reality(tm)&quot;/&quot;everything that exist&quot;.<br /> (...)<br /> But even if they do have a pet theory that explains everything they do (that was more common in 2nd ed than nowdays, as Five Eyes said), that's not to say that they believe what they do can be explained within the framework of current science. </div> </div> </div>You are right. I should have said that it's part of science. My point is the Scientist will have an explanation that is in conformity with Science. This means that he must have a verydetailed &quot;why&quot; otherwise it will go to the field of Magick, which is what the character kinda do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, that's more polemical. And I will elaborate on this latter<br /> (...)<br /> Hermetics (and Verbena) are <b>aesthetically </b>the closest to being wizardly wizards. Even the intelectual outlook of the Hermetics it's very D&amp;D wizard themed (unsurprising, since they come from Ars Magica, and Ars had as one of it's goals to remake the &quot;old timer&quot; D&amp;D image of wizards w/o arbitrary limitations like being unable to cast in armor). </div> </div> </div>Ok, you were talking about classic Merlin (D&amp;D) mage. I wasn't. Not specifically this kind of mage, although this surely fit, afterall it's the classical mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What you've just said it's empty of <b>aesthetic</b>. It's formless and thus says nothing about your character:<br /> <br /> &quot;he uses his very own counsciousness and Will to change reality&quot;.<br /> Everyone does that, literally means nothing. </div> </div> </div>Hmm. They do in a sense.YEs, the thing about mages is that they are changing reality with their Will, but they don't know that. I described the character paradigm, it is the mixture of 2 or 3 paradigms that we have in M20. How is that empty?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;To me, a mage is someone that cast spells, that works with energies or things that are arcane, unknown. &quot;<br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Now, that may be of interest: But what IS this &quot;casting spells&quot; you're talking about? .</span><br /> <br /> An Etherite won't be caught dead chanting an enochian incantation w/o some theory about why that works...<b>but</b><b>, as described,</b><b> neither will your character.</b> You stated, very clearly, that <i>your character doesn't place any value on those &quot;Instruments&quot;</i>, <i>they aren't MAGICAL!</i>. They are merely<i> a tool to chanel your mental power in order to weave the <b>&quot;totally not ether&quot; </b>field into phenomena</i>. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the character won't be chanting enochian incantations, but that's not because he doesn't belive in magick. It's because he doesn't believe in the power of symbolism, other than to focus the mind. candles don't have power, circles don't have power and incantations don't have power other than helping the other mage to do exactly what my char does with his body and energy (which could perfectly be the Ether): align their counsciousness and Will with that of the universe and change things for what they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's what an Etherite would say (except he would be manipulating the &quot;ether field&quot; rather than the &quot;not ether field&quot;) </div> </div> </div>No, the Etherite wouldn't sufice to say that he's just using the power of his Will. Well, he could but wouldn't that make a shitty Etherite? Take &quot;scientists&quot; from our real life that get one quantum mechanics theory and begins to make mental gymnastics to explain parapsychology. How are they viewed in the scientific community?<br /> <br /> So, the problem with the Etherite is that he would [b]have/[b] to have a good scientific explanation, which I don't want the char to have because he's not that good of a scientist and he . And if he stays in that shallow explanations, then he'd be a joke for the Tradition. And certainly an empty character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mystics, even Chaos Magicians, think their magical spells are magical. Chaos Magicians believe that the power of their symbols comes from the fact that these matter to them and to others. They have power because they are a placeholder of the Will manifested trough their own lives and those of the people that surrounds them (hence why Chaos Mages use pop culture symbols so much, they are already *charged* with magick in their worldview because they matter to a lot of people). As simplified as Chaos Magick it's, it still places more importance on the symbols as placeholders of the Will than your mage that uses them as a mere way to focus that <s>psionic power</s> Will, and denies them any sort of magick outside of his use.<br /> <br /> If you want to sell me a Chaos Magician, <i>aesthetically</i>, there needs to be less emphasis on the pseudo-scientific theories about why magick stuff *really* works and more emphasis on the <b>arcane/esoteric/mystical </b>side of how magick stuff *really* works . </div> </div> </div>I agree only with one little &quot;but&quot;. The Chaos Magician do not believe in the power of the symbols, but in the power of belief. Which needs not to be a symbol or any form of &quot;classic&quot; ritual. I'd say Chaos Magick is quite opposite to High Ritual. Chaos Magick don't care for details, symbolisms or materials. Anything, as long as the mage believes, works. M20 even uses &quot;raising and directing personal energy (that is, Quintessence) through extreme experiences&quot; which is what my char is doing.<br /> <br /> The character just can't explain scientifically exactly how/why his powers works. That's why he considers himself as a mage. He's using unknown (arcane) energy. He is shaping Reality by aligning with the universe itself. How is that too much focus on pseudo-scientific theories and less on arcane/mystical?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not to say you can't <i>reason </i>why these work and try to apply the scientific method, it's just that these &quot;mystical spells&quot; need to be more the focus of the character and less of a meaningless word to declare an Effect </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate more? The focus of the character is completely mystical, the only thing that is more scientifical is the &quot;Psionics&quot; practice and the &quot;Counsciousness reality&quot; (that goes in hand with &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot;), all the others focus are mystical. And yes, having a mystical focus that is reasoned and applied scientific method is eactly what I look for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T16:06:05-08:00","id":1350335,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Five Eyes;n1350306]I'm of the opinion that no Hermetic gets out of their apprenticeship without learning the core of the Hermetic style, as learning the three types of magic &quot;in proper order&quot; is seen as important. As the RevTradBook notes that even Ex Misc, where all the weirdos are, funnels <i>everyone </i>through the high ritual practice, I see no reason to think the example Tytalus athlete is somehow not using the usual Hermetic instruments and practices. This accords with the style described in the prior material and in the Rev corebook, and with M20's entry.[/uqote]<br /> <br /> I see, and do you believe that all Hermetics that are in the order entered this way or is possible for a mage to join the order already being awakened? Also, it is quite hard to mix High Ritual with using a body as instrument. Possible, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hermetics think magic is part of nature, too - every spell is the consequence of occult laws of sympathy, resonance, and essence. This is sort of where I've been stumbling - high ritual isn't superstitious or faith-based. It's very practical and rigorous. The planet Mercury, quartz crystals, and the color red have certain properties. Through Will, you harness them. Even linear sorcerers, with no mastery of their Will, can manage this - wands actually do stuff. (If they didn't, there would be no reason to keep dangerous occult secrets <i>secret</i>.) Remember, the Hermetic description isn't &quot;the gods are mere notions which let me focus my Will.&quot; Rather, it's &quot;with sufficient Will, I will order the gods to act, and they will do as I say.&quot; </div> </div> </div>You are right. But what about a non high ritual practicant Hermetic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does your character differentiate an &quot;energy&quot; which responds to &quot;consciousness and desire&quot;, and Etherites claiming &quot;psychic power&quot; can alter the physical world? Like, how would this character describe how he can create or direct electricity with &quot;desire&quot;? Is he saying this &quot;energy field&quot; can generate some undocumented force which leaves his brain and then goes to influence the movement of electrical charge? By what mechanism? How is adding entities to the scientific corpus in this way any different than what an Etherite does?<br /> <br /> Is the goal some sort of &quot;mystic&quot; character who has no &quot;mystical&quot; beliefs? Or just no beliefs they can't articulate in language which would look acceptably &quot;scientific&quot; to a normal Sleeper? </div> </div> </div>The core of his paradigm is that the universe and counsciousness are one. Your Will can make changes in all that Chaos. He does that by focusing into that energy (Quintessence, Ether, Chi, whatever) using his instruments (the 7 I listed). So it's like Counsciousness -&gt; Energy -&gt; Instruments, one supporting the other until Reality is changed.<br /> <br /> He would explain an Etherite psychich power without much advanced explanations, he is doing the same as him. As I said, he could definitely be an Etherite, but a shitty one, because he rellies so much in the unknown, the arcane, the mystic. Aren't the focus I posted mystics?<br /> Couldn't understan your last question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T02:48:39-08:00","id":1350412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350335#post1350335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see, and do you believe that all Hermetics that are in the order entered this way or is possible for a mage to join the order already being awakened?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can join the order while Awakened, or Awaken &quot;early&quot; in your apprenticeship, but doing so doesn't seem to let you skip any of the curriculum - the RevTradbook notes apprenticeship is often <i>more </i>grueling for people who come to the table already Awakened. Those first three stages are when you learn the foundations of the Hermetic art and are subjected to tests of erudition and character. Based on the older material, I suspect an Awakened apprentice would be required to go through the motions of learning the most basic magics first - the Order thinks &quot;jumping ahead&quot; will stunt a mage's development and make them passive and Will-less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it is quite hard to mix High Ritual with using a body as instrument. Possible, though. ... But what about a non high ritual practicant Hermetic? </div> </div> </div>I think the same foundation basically holds for Hermetic alchemists and the various more exotic Ex Misc people - even if their magic is unorthodox <i>by Hermetic standards, </i>they're still members of the Tradition, and share its core philosophy, with magic based on &quot;ancient and arcane rituals&quot; using &quot;elemental forces through incantations, signs, seals, paraphernalia, and secret languages.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Hermetic athlete-mage like the Olympian example character might use high ritual magic to draw power into their body through particular grueling postures, fasting regimens during key astrological phases, ritual purification with water, etc. They might call divine energies into themselves through incantations to Hermes or Hercules or inscribe runes into their kit. If alchemy's more their thing, they might refine potions to increase their strength or purge the body of toxins, or create incense which provokes a winning mind-state or revitalizes aching muscles. There's an antique magical practice which uses quotations from the works of Homer as incantations - a great fit for any academic, but particularly for that particular example character. A Tytalus mage might shade more into the practice M20 calls dominion, winning a wrestling match (in a re-enactment of any number of godly struggles) to cow an opponent or affirm and enhance their own physical power. Importantly, a lot of this &quot;clean ritual living&quot; can be done <i>before </i>you need it, as long as you maintain your regimen (like any good athlete.) A theurge-athlete might abstain from meat to maintain their body's purity as a potential vessel for god-forms, whether those forms are traditional or Chaotic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The core of his paradigm is that the universe and counsciousness are one. Your Will can make changes in all that Chaos. He does that by focusing into that energy (Quintessence, Ether, Chi, whatever) using his instruments (the 7 I listed). So it's like Counsciousness -&gt; Energy -&gt; Instruments, one supporting the other until Reality is changed.<br /> He would explain an Etherite psychich power without much advanced explanations, he is doing the same as him. As I said, he could definitely be an Etherite, but a shitty one, because he rellies so much in the unknown, the arcane, the mystic. Aren't the focus I posted mystics? </div> </div> </div>I don't see how the practices are inherently mystical if the character denies any mystical system of explanation or &quot;superstitious&quot; concepts. If &quot;chaos magic&quot; just means &quot;strong mental images&quot; and the unstated &quot;force&quot; is, per the character, some sort of undiscovered energy harnessed by provoking the brain to use its psychic powers... where's the mysticism? The whole structure is &quot;unscientific&quot; in the sense that it contains energies which don't match up with Sleeper science, but with very few tweaks this setup could be a Technocrat - they do stuff Sleeper science can't explain, too.<br /> <br /> Proponents of the pseudoscience of &quot;new thought&quot; think that, by clearly imagining what you desire, you can attract it to you - so if you want a job, meditating on it will cause the universe to give you a job. Is this what the character means by &quot;Will&quot;? I.e. They just need to concentrate on what they desire hard enough, and it will happen?<br /> <br /> (If nothing else, this conversation is reaffirming my feeling that much of M20's Focus material should just be dumpstered.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T15:56:20-08:00","id":1350717,"title":"","content":"I think we shouldn't be so serious about that entry in M20. Otherwise <b>all</b> Hermetics would use just HR,Alchemy and dominion. This would leave no room for character development, as you can get as much as 3 practices.<br /> Also, aside from that single frase, there is no evidence that all Hermetics have to use those practices other than the description of apprenticeship in trad book (when focus worked completely differently). <br /> I'd say it's like saying Akashics have to have Do. The majority do, but if you match their mindset you will be welcomed in the Tradition.<br /> The core of Hermetic belief isn't High Ritual, that's their most common practice. The core of their belief is <b>Will</b>. As rev. Trad book shows us:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tradition Book pg63:<br /> &quot;The essence of Hermetic belief comes down to a sinhle concept: the ascendancy of the Will. The Order of Hermes, more than any other mystic fellowship (even the Conventions of the Technocracy), believes that the power to shape reality stems solely from the wellsprings of Awakened human consciousness and the resolve to enforce the dictates of that consciousness.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That is exactly what my char believes and do, only with a little touch of scientific background, which is completely acceptable in the Order.<br /> In fact, the strong Will, the study, the determination, the rational mind is also very well looked by the Order.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350412#post1350412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can join the order while Awakened, or Awaken &quot;early&quot; in your apprenticeship, but doing so doesn't seem to let you skip any of the curriculum - the RevTradbook notes apprenticeship is often <i>more </i>grueling for people who come to the table already Awakened. Those first three stages are when you learn the foundations of the Hermetic art and are subjected to tests of erudition and character. Based on the older material, I suspect an Awakened apprentice would be required to go through the motions of learning the most basic magics first - the Order thinks &quot;jumping ahead&quot; will stunt a mage's development and make them passive and Will-less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe a mage that not only awoke, but already has knowledge enough to be on the 4th stage (1st dot in Forces), where you are considered a full mage wouldn't have to go through all thr steps of learning magick, this makes no sense.<br /> He might, maybe, go to learn about Hermetics history, laws, etc. But magick os already established for this one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I I don't see how the practices are inherently mystical if the character denies any mystical system of explanation or &quot;superstitious&quot; concepts. If &quot;chaos magic&quot; just means &quot;strong mental images&quot; and the unstated &quot;force&quot; is, per the character, some sort of undiscovered energy harnessed by provoking the brain to use its psychic powers... where's the mysticism? The whole structure is &quot;unscientific&quot; in the sense that it contains energies which don't match up with Sleeper science, but with very few tweaks this setup could be a Technocrat - they do stuff Sleeper science can't explain, too.<br /> <br /> Proponents of the pseudoscience of &quot;new thought&quot; think that, by clearly imagining what you desire, you can attract it to you - so if you want a job, meditating on it will cause the universe to give you a job. Is this what the character means by &quot;Will&quot;? I.e. They just need to concentrate on what they desire hard enough, and it will happen?<br /> <br /> (If nothing else, this conversation is reaffirming my feeling that much of M20's Focus material should just be dumpstered.) </div> </div> </div>With very few tweaks I could make him an Akashic, or a Technoract or maybe a Verbena.<br /> He does not deny the mystic view of it, he still think he's performing magick. A scientist would not believe that you can teleport with the power of your consciousness alone. There's no brain wave involved. I consider it mystic because there is no plausible explanation that a Scientisr that is worth what he eats would give. <br /> <br /> Again, you seem to be confusing high ritual with paradigm. You don't need to believe in symbolisms to be considered mystic. What's more mystic than consider that your very mind and consciousness is part of the universe itself?<br /> <br /> Will is stronger and more complex than simple desire. Also, this is the law of attraction and we could say that &quot;As above, so bellow&quot; could fit very well in his view of mind and universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-24T17:34:31-08:00","id":1350738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350717#post1350717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we shouldn't be so serious about that entry in M20. Otherwise <b>all</b> Hermetics would use just HR,Alchemy and dominion. This would leave no room for character development, as you can get as much as 3 practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Hermetic <i>lacks training </i>in HR, Alchemy, and Dominion, which isn't the same as being obligated to use all three of them to define your character's Focus. This matches up with their presentation in their Tradition Books, as I have noted.The M20 Book of Secrets notes that the Hermetics are highly regimented in their chosen instruments, and:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Focus entry on each two-page spread of Mage 20 describes the preferred focus<br /> of the metaphysical society in question, and although certain<br /> individual variations are allowed \u2013 say, a Verbena witch using a<br /> computer \u2013 members of that society employ most, if not all, of<br /> the focus elements mentioned within that entry.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Focus entry appears to be a broad description of the <i>scope </i>of things the faction teaches, trains in, and believes. Your Practices are chosen from the list, but the Focus is an arch-category describing the beliefs and practices of the group's membership, such that they can accommodate (and may have trained in) any part of the list.<br /> <br /> It's like the &quot;language&quot; the faction speaks in. You could make a Dreamspeaker without shamanism as part of their Practice, but shamanism is part of the Dreamspeaker paradigm - a High Ritual Dreamspeaker would be using those rituals to contact and commune with the spirits, right? Every Hermetic is trained in the occult laws which underpin HR and Alchemy, and even a Martial Artist Hermetic is going to be interpreting Martial Arts through the lens of the study of alchemy. Even if they never pick up a flask or otherwise have Alchemy as one of their Practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350717#post1350717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, aside from that single frase, there is no evidence that all Hermetics have to use those practices other than the description of apprenticeship in trad book (when focus worked completely differently). I'd say it's like saying Akashics have to have Do. The majority do, but if you match their mindset you will be welcomed in the Tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per M20, which is a paraphrase of Mage 2nd edition, Hermetics &quot;master ancient and arcane rituals through constant study and intense practice. Tapping elemental currents through incantations, signs, seals, paraphernalia, and secret languages...&quot; Both Tradbooks and their entries in prior corebooks also emphasize how ritual performance and occult energies are the heart of Hermetic magic. Even the chaos magicians in the sect are doing so &quot;filtered through&quot; the strong &quot;trunk of Hermeticism&quot;, specifically &quot;Hermetic high ritual magick.&quot;<br /> <br /> Do is described as &quot;integral&quot; to Akashic magic in their Tradbook, in fact - not every Akashic has Martial Arts as a practice, but every Akashic is trained in the <i>philosophy </i>behind Do, and uses that to perform their magic. It's part of the beliefs of the Tradition, which are a layer slightly above (or surrounding) Focus.<br /> <br /> Why do the Hermetics keep occult lore secret if, as you are trying to argue, they know the occult lore doesn't do anything?<br /> Why does the Book of Secrets say this about the Order of Hermes:<i> &quot;one does not, for instance, use the Fifth Pentacle of the Sun when summoning demons. (One uses the Fifth Pentacle of Mars\u2026 among other precautions.)&quot;</i> When the Hermetics supposedly don't believe specific pentacles matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350717#post1350717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe a mage that not only awoke, but already has knowledge enough to be on the 4th stage (1st dot in Forces), where you are considered a full mage wouldn't have to go through all the steps of learning magick, this makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's pretty normal, really - the Hermetics think you have to learn magic in a certain way, in a certain order, to know how to do it <b>right</b>. Think of a gifted street performer coming to study at a ballet academy. You start from square one, because whatever you learned about dancing on the street, that's now how Proper Dancing works. An Awakened apprentice is worse than one with no training - they've had a chance to learn bad habits. Their pater has to beat those out of them. Why would the Hermetics give full initiate status - and therefore full citizenship in the Order - to someone who has not been properly trained and vetted?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350717#post1350717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He does not deny the mystic view of it, he still think he's performing magick. A scientist would not believe that you can teleport with the power of your consciousness alone. There's no brain wave involved. I consider it mystic because there is no plausible explanation that a Scientisr that is worth what he eats would give.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your character believes a thing a &quot;scientist&quot; would not (that he can &quot;teleport with the power of consciousness alone&quot;), why are you saying &quot;He is still a scientist and everything he does has a good scientifically explanation&quot;?<br /> <br /> They're a mystic because they do things which they accept don't have a scientific explanation, but &quot;everything he does has a good scientific explanation&quot;? Which is it?<br /> <br /> Is anyone who doesn't have a scientific explanation for magic a mystic? Or is it that anyone who believes in magic is a mystic?<br /> <br /> Part of what makes this concept feel nebulous to me - and possibly &quot;hollow&quot; to Aleph - is how the guy doesn't seem to believe or posit anything. The concept unfolds backwards from &quot;can do magic&quot; and seems preoccupied with &quot;and makes no claims about it.&quot; Their magic Just Works, and they arrive at the most abstract (pseudo-Purple) description possible - something which, to me, doesn't really register as a small-p paradigm. In M20, where belief is the lever that makes magick work, a character who only believes &quot;magic works&quot; is stuck in a recursive loop","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T06:17:47-08:00","id":1350804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350738#post1350738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No Hermetic <i>lacks training </i>in HR, Alchemy, and Dominion, which isn't the same as being obligated to use all three of them to define your character's Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the Hermetic proceeds to spend years of painful training and study of HR,Alchemy and Dominion just to learn them and then, after having this knowledge, he drops all this shit and goes training martial arts? <br /> <br /> So, in order to not completely restrict Hermetics to those 3 practices you habe two options, or he picks another one and blend it into those 3, having a total of 4, which is very confusing and unrealistic. Or you forget all that study and pick 1-3 new practices, which is also unrealistic and might end up with 6 practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This matches up with their presentation in their Tradition Books, as I have noted.The M20 Book of Secrets notes that the Hermetics are highly regimented in their chosen instruments, and:<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The Focus entry on each two-page spread of Mage 20 describes the preferred focus<br /> of the metaphysical society in question, and although certain<br /> individual variations are allowed \u2013 say, a Verbena witch using a<br /> computer \u2013 members of that society employ most, if not all, of<br /> the focus elements mentioned within that entry.&amp;quot; </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know and understand that the majority of members of a Tradition will use the focus list. But M20 always states pretty clearly that there are exceptions and &quot;individual variations&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, you are forgetting that, while those 3 practices are present in their <b>training</b>, the real core and important aspect of Hermetics is Will, and their notion that they are the source of the power.<br /> <br /> As in M20 description &quot;Hermetic with firm Will commands, \u2018Do!\u2019 And it is done.\u201d&quot;<br /> And &quot;This age\u2019s Hermetics are rolling up their sleeves and remaking the Order from its foundations while keeping those foundations \u2013 confidence, knowledge, excellence, and Will \u2013 intact&quot;<br /> <br /> Confidence,knowledge,excellence and Will. Those are the foundations of the Order and my char have all of them. Also, I already posted the Trad book entry where it describes the very core of Hermetic belief, which matches exactly my char's.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Focus entry appears to be a broad description of the <i>scope </i>of things the faction teaches, trains in, and believes. Your Practices are chosen from the list, but the Focus is an arch-category describing the beliefs and practices of the group's membership, such that they can accommodate (and may have trained in) any part of the list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like the &amp;quot;language&amp;quot; the faction speaks in. You could make a Dreamspeaker without shamanism as part of their Practice, but shamanism is part of the Dreamspeaker paradigm - a High Ritual Dreamspeaker would be using those rituals to contact and commune with the spirits, right? Every Hermetic is trained in the occult laws which underpin HR and Alchemy, and even a Martial Artist Hermetic is going to be interpreting Martial Arts through the lens of the study of alchemy. Even if they never pick up a flask or otherwise have Alchemy as one of their Practices. </div> </div> </div>Now you are just wrong. If you character do not have alchemy (even that mixed with other practices) he won't use any alchemy principle. You are confusing Tradition with belief. <br /> A Tradition is just an organized group that share the same concept in a broad way. No 2 mages have the exact same belief and if your character do not share any characteristics with his Tradition he would just be an outcast or invited to a more fitting Tradition. <br /> <br /> A lazzy ass, dumb mage, or one that doesn't share any aspect of their paradigms would not mske a good Hermetic. That is not the case. My char has the exact core concept of the Tradition and share one practice (Chaos Magick). He might not be the classic Hermetic, be he would be easily accepted there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do the Hermetics keep occult lore secret if, as you are trying to argue, they know the occult lore doesn't do anything?<br /> Why does the Book of Secrets say this about the Order of Hermes:<i> &amp;quot;one does not, for instance, use the Fifth Pentacle of the Sun when summoning demons. (One uses the Fifth Pentacle of Mars\u2026 among other precautions.)&amp;quot;</i> When the Hermetics supposedly don't believe specific pentacles matter? </div> </div> </div>Every mage is different and while there are ones who believes in the intrinsic power of the tool, there are others that knows the power is in fact their Will.<br /> Nevertheless, even the mage that believe in thr power of Will knows that he must use his instruments right. He won't be able to focus his intent just right if he's using the instrument just for the fun of it. Unless he dropped that instrument he still give importance to it, he just understand that the real source of power os himself. He still <b>needs</b> to use them right, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's pretty normal, really - the Hermetics think you have to learn magic in a certain way, in a certain order, to know how to do it <b>right</b>. Think of a gifted street performer coming to study at a ballet academy. You start from square one, because whatever you learned about dancing on the street, that's now how Proper Dancing works. An Awakened apprentice is worse than one with no training - they've had a chance to learn bad habits. Their pater has to beat those out of them. Why would the Hermetics give full initiate status - and therefore full citizenship in the Order - to someone who has not been properly trained and vetted? </div> </div> </div>Mages chsnge tradition all the time, are you saying that every mage that comes to the Order needs to go through training from the beggining?<br /> A full mage (Arete 1 and 1 Sphere)that want to join the Order and has the Hermetic hubris would not want to join the kids class (sleepers apprentices). <br /> Let me ask this, a mage with Arete 3 and 7 or 8 sphere dots (lvl 6 in Hermeric hierarchy) would join the apprentices too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your character believes a thing a &amp;quot;scientist&amp;quot; would not (that he can &amp;quot;teleport with the power of consciousness alone&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, why are you saying &amp;quot;He is still a scientist and everything he does has a good scientifically explanation&amp;quot;?<br /> They're a mystic because they do things which they accept don't have a scientific explanation, but &amp;quot;everything he does has a good scientific explanation&amp;quot;? Which is it </div> </div> </div>You are right to be confused, I am not being clear, sorry.<br /> First, he doesn't believe that he can teleport with the power of consciousness alone. Consciousness being related with the universe is what let's him do it with the help of his practices+instruments. Those practices and the very belief of Will is not scientific, since he can't explain it in a scientific way.<br /> However he is sn engineer and a scientific mind in the sense that tries to study magick behaviour, he believes in atoms, cells, electromagnetism, periodic table, etc. All Sleeper science. He also use it to explain his effects, he wouldn't get invisible because an angel blow on him, instead he would bend the light around him or turn his body composition in a way that it become transparent.<br /> What I mean is, while the source of his power is mystical and unexplainable scientifically, his effects and behaviour towards magick is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is anyone who doesn't have a scientific explanation for magic a mystic? Or is it that anyone who believes in magic is a mystic? </div> </div> </div>I'd say both. To be a Scientist you have to see effects as a procedure, not magick. And for thst you have to have clear understanding and explanation for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Part of what makes this concept feel nebulous to me - and possibly &amp;quot;hollow&amp;quot; to Aleph - is how the guy doesn't seem to believe or posit anything. The concept unfolds backwards from &amp;quot;can do magic&amp;quot; and seems preoccupied with &amp;quot;and makes no claims about it.&amp;quot; Their magic Just Works, and they arrive at the most abstract (pseudo-Purple) description possible - something which, to me, doesn't really register as a small-p paradigm. In M20, where belief is the lever that makes magick work, a character who only believes &amp;quot;magic works&amp;quot; is stuck in a recursive loop </div> </div> </div>I don't understand. What else would you add, considering everything I posted and using those paradigms, practices and instruments? <br /> <br /> Also, if you were to make it an Etherite, how would you give a &quot;mage&quot; flavour (if possible) and would he be casting spells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-25T18:13:30-08:00","id":1350938,"title":"","content":"The Hermetic curriculum includes their laws, philosophy, history, and their <i>foundational magical texts</i>. Those texts cover the concepts involved in the Practices which M20 and Revised say are universal. I don't find it credible to argue that a character who rejects Hermetic spiritual beliefs and magical theory has &quot;knowledge&quot;, as far as the Hermetics are concerned. They're ignorant of the true nature of reality and humanity.<br /> <br /> A Syndicate money-man is confident, knowledgeable (about accountancy and finance), excellent at his job, and demonstrably Willful - he's a mage, after all. Is he a model Hermetic? Is the only difference between a Syndicate financier and a Hermetic &quot;acknowledging that I am the source of my own power&quot;? The egocentric Syndicate produces a lot of people who think that, even if they don't call it Will.<br /> <br /> (And no, I don't think there's much reason to think mages get to skip steps. For your example of a Disciple with many Sphere dots, absolutely not - a Hermetic of that rank is <i>expected to train apprentices. </i>The Order of Hermes thinks other Traditions <i>do magic wrong. </i>They're not going to leave the task of teaching the next generation of Hermetics to someone who, by their measure, dropped out of high school.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350804#post1350804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lazzy ass, dumb mage, or one that doesn't share any aspect of their paradigms would not mske a good Hermetic. That is not the case. My char has the exact core concept of the Tradition and share one practice (Chaos Magick). He might not be the classic Hermetic, be he would be easily accepted there.</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone can't manage to make sense of the <i>corpus Hermeticum </i>and is ignorant of the basics behind alchemy, by Hermetic standards, they <i>are </i>a lazy dumbass. People who have not been properly initiated are intellectual and moral children<i>, </i>no matter how much worldly power they wield - even if that power is magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350804#post1350804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the Hermetic proceeds to spend years of painful training and study of HR,Alchemy and Dominion just to learn them and then, after having this knowledge, he drops all this shit and goes training martial arts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of - I think a Hermetic Martial Artist practices <i>Hermetic Martial Arts</i>. They undergo their training, understand the occult rules and symbolic systems which govern Hermetic magic (the Hermetic paradigm, in a Revised sense), and then adopt their intellectual tradition to new methods, or choose to focus on particular elements of some part of their training. Every Hermetic is practicing magic through that lens, just as a hypertech Verbena or Chorister is practicing their technology <i>through </i>their Tradition's over-arching Focus. Most real-world chaos magicians first learned in a more rigorous ritual practice or a more dogmatic religion.<br /> <br /> Consider how Hermetic mages who use technology apply their prior ritual knowledge to hypertech Practices or paradigms like &quot;Everything is Data&quot;. Verditus mages don't mean the same thing as Virtual Adepts do when they talk about &quot;information.&quot; Each Tradition has a culture, that's the point of the section of the Book of Secrets I highlighted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350804#post1350804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, you are forgetting that, while those 3 practices are present in their <b>training</b>, the real core and important aspect of Hermetics is Will, and their notion that they are the source of the power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really important. Or meaningfully distinct from the Euthanatos or Choristers. Hermetic Will isn't Purple. It's a model for egocentric, spiritually-assertive praxis, the consequence of a human-centric spiritual philosophy. Even the <i>enfants terrible </i>in House Ex Misc are operating from these principles.<br /> <br /> An improperly-trained mage lacks a disciplined Will. Someone who wants to &quot;skip ahead&quot; to magia without the proper spiritual and intellectual training isn't going to be accepted as an apprentice, much less an Initiate - even if they can do magic, they're not doing it <i>right. </i>If they're claiming to be using their Will, who cares? It's like watching a guy borrow quantum mechanics terms to try and sell you a magnetic bracelet - the Order says &quot;without proper Hermetic education, you can't actually know your own Will.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350804#post1350804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, he doesn't believe that he can teleport with the power of consciousness alone. Consciousness being related with the universe is what let's him do it with the help of his practices+instruments. Those practices and the very belief of Will is not scientific, since he can't explain it in a scientific way.<br /> However he is sn engineer and a scientific mind in the sense that tries to study magick behaviour, he believes in atoms, cells, electromagnetism, periodic table, etc. All Sleeper science. He also use it to explain his effects, he wouldn't get invisible because an angel blow on him, instead he would bend the light around him or turn his body composition in a way that it become transparent.<br /> What I mean is, while the source of his power is mystical and unexplainable scientifically, his effects and behaviour towards magick is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, this is something I can talk about more clearly.<br /> <br /> Compare your character to these two examples. Both are designed to use similar Practices/Paradigms to your proposal, and to be similar to each other in ways I hope will illuminate how their Traditional beliefs shine through despite similar backgrounds and theories. I also threw in a science-background Hermetic and a low-devices Etherite.<br /> <br /> Where I find your example character's Focus to be, for lack of a better word, facile is in the transition between Instrument to Practice to Paradigm. How does a rational, scientifically-minded person describe the energies their Instruments are helping them channel? How do those energies change the world? Where do they come from - are they created by the brain, or some sort of psychic <i>nous </i>which isn't biological in nature? In a worked example, what do they think happens when they use their Focus to, say, become invisible with Forces or read someone's memories with Mind? This is the stuff a small-p-paradigm is about<b></b>: What sort of entities exist in the world, and how do they act upon one another. What <i>is </i>Quintessence, and why does chaos magic help focus and channel it?<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Scientist Sven</b> is an Etherite who believes in a distributed psychic consciousness-field, from which Reality emerges (&quot;Everything is Chaos.&quot;). He believes humans have psychic powers, mostly used subconsciously (to create Reality, including its various Realms, gods, and demons), but which can be used actively to tweak Reality by Awakened minds. His Practices are Psionics and Chaos Magick, and his Instruments include gesture, eye contact, and meditation. He can use eye contact and concentration to read people's thoughts (Mind), strongly envision an object's purpose in order to endow it with agency (Spirit), or use a closed body posture (like a boxer's guard) to concentrate on not being seen, causing light to bend around him (Forces invisibility). He can describe these effects scientifically - the data in someone's mind can be understood as physical signals and interpreted, and he agrees that what he's doing is affecting the behavior of visible light. His causes are &quot;unscientific&quot;, in that Sleeper science does not believe in them, but they are expressed &quot;scientifically&quot; in that he thinks they're rational, physical properties of the brain - the untapped telepathic and telekinetic potential present in all human brains.<br /> <br /> Sven thinks his effects can't be replicated by machines or devices alone - they're the product of the unique properties of his Awakened brain and mental discipline. He has a rigid paradigm, and thinks that Enochian chants, ecstatic states, and the mandalas used by other Traditions are ways to tap this psionic potential, which various cultures discovered independently. He thinks his method is best, and the other approaches are either overly-elaborate or have dangerous side effects. (Sven could fit in as a slightly radical Technocrat, in a pinch, and is kind of not a great Scientist by Etherite standards, though in a way he is not likely to get called on.)<br /> <br /> <b>Fiona Flambeau</b> is a Hermetic with a PHD in physics. She was recruited out of her lab work and trained by her mater. She believes natural laws govern the cosmos (&quot;A Mechanistic Cosmos&quot;), with Sleeper science covering only a small portion of them - and Hermetic magic drawing on those as of yet not understood. Over the course of her training, she studied sciences adjacent to the occult principles she was learning, such as alchemy, early modern medicine, and parapsychology. She does not believe in absolute occult symbols, but rather holds the archetypes behind ritual magic to be well-established conceptual aggregates - she believes in the power of angels and Enochian chants, but they were made powerful by Man, not God. She uses incantations, artwork, amulets, and brews and potions as her instruments to gather and direct her personal psychic energies and the power of these archetypes.<br /> <br /> Her Practices are Chaos Magick, Alchemy, and Psionics - she can extend her psychic aura through imbibing alchemical potions or performing repetitive incantations, and taps into archetypical sources of power with amulets and artwork. This allows her to commune with spiritual intelligences or ghosts (Spirit), light fires pyrokinetically (Forces), or call upon Raziel, the angel of secrets, to conceal herself from sight (Forces or Mind.) She believes spiritual ephemera and psychic energy to be states of matter or types of energy science has yet to discover, can describe how her potions are designed to stimulate the parts of the brain associated with psychic phenomena, and acknowledges how Raziel's influence is occluding light by acting on it in a way physics can describe - it's just that these physical things are governed by more laws than Sleeper science is aware of. (She thinks a truly enlightened society would regard physics as applied metaphysics, just as biology is the &quot;result&quot; of chemistry.)<br /> <br /> Fiona has what Mage calls an &quot;Open&quot; paradigm. She thinks other people are wrong about what Gods are, but she admits that her interpretation and approach may only be best <i>for her. </i>She's a critical thinker and is reasonable enough to be suspicious of her own theories - part of her Flambeau commitment to truth and light includes not lying to herself or being ignorant of her own biases.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 11-25-2019, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T05:10:23-08:00","id":1351015,"title":"","content":"Nice examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine he's first presenting to the Etherites:<br /> <br /> - Ok, you say you are able to create fire just by the use of your mind, how does it works?<br /> -I don't know, I just know it is related to my counsciousness being one with Reality and capable of shapping it.<br /> -Nonsene! Are you using you cerebral waves to vibrate quantum particles in a high frequency to make the comburent catch fire?<br /> -Dude, I'm just focusing my Will into th..<br /> -Get the fuck outta my face!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>-Wait, let's not forget that he has &quot;machines&quot; as Instrument, I'm sure we can work with that: Albeit he's too lazzy to tell us *how* do they work to enhance his Will (or to manipulate the Force?), I'm sure we can squeeze a theory that's more than repeating the word Will over and over...<br /> <br /> ...if only because machines have to *do* something mechanical or physical that &quot;works&quot; on that Will/counsciousness (or on the Force?) somehow, and properly explaining *that* undoubtedly requires more than one single syllable, and perhaps some &quot;real&quot; words like brain, nervous system, psychosomatic, or a formula to explain how mechanisms and mundane energies could relate to the Force. Maybe even the word Ether, that we like so much<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, the Etherite wouldn't sufice to say that he's just using the power of his Will. Well, he could but wouldn't that make a shitty Etherite? Take &quot;scientists&quot; from our real life that get one quantum mechanics theory and begins to make mental gymnastics to explain parapsychology. How are they viewed in the scientific community? </div> </div> </div>Like Etherites?<br /> <br /> Don't make things harder than they are. For most Etherite characters, saying the word &quot;Ether&quot; suffices to explain most things (the classic Ether Goggles come to mind. You can use them as Instrument to see anything, why?, because Ether). If you're altering the etheric waveform with your honed psionic powers, that's something Etherites can understand.<br /> <br /> Other Etherites aren't going to complain because your theory isn't solid or scientific enough, Etherites may think your Science! it's <i>boring, </i>and doesn't deserve the apostrophe, because it's too all encompassing and leaves little space for maths and actual engineering.<br /> <br /> ...but, on the other hand: As Five Eyes points out, Hermetics will refuse to grant you the title of &quot;<i>mage</i>&quot;, you're to be treated like an apprentice until you learn ALL of their curriculum, the wizardly symbolisms that your character dislikes (even if you refuse to use them as Instrument). And you're not going to be popular there either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-26-2019, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T07:38:08-08:00","id":1351037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1350938#post1350938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hermetic curriculum includes their laws, philosophy, history, and their <i>foundational magical texts</i>. Those texts cover the concepts involved in the Practices which M20 and Revised say are universal. I don't find it credible to argue that a character who rejects Hermetic spiritual beliefs and magical theory has &amp;quot;knowledge&amp;quot;, as far as the Hermetics are concerned. They're ignorant of the true nature of reality and humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you\u2019re mistaken. It is very rare that 2 mages have the exactly same paradigm. There are lots of different beliefs inside a single Tradition. You also seem to be too rigid about their training. Knowledge comes in many ways and Hermetics seems to praise all kinds (the books don\u2019t even restrict to magickl knowledge). Also, what is knowledge for one mage might be bullshit for another, this is dependent of paradigm and we know this happens in any Tradition.<br /> Again, a Tradition is nothing more than an organized group that share the same concept in a broad way. You just have to match some of their traits and beliefs. You don\u2019t need to be the example role of a Hermetic to be accepted.<br /> One more point, you think in a time of need like the Ascension war, the Order would dump a good, intelligent, determined, Willed mage because of some minor differences or lack of formal training?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Syndicate money-man is confident, knowledgeable (about accountancy and finance), excellent at his job, and demonstrably Willful - he's a mage, after all. Is he a model Hermetic? Is the only difference between a Syndicate financier and a Hermetic &amp;quot;acknowledging that I am the source of my own power&amp;quot;? The egocentric Syndicate produces a lot of people who think that, even if they don't call it Will. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not. Tell me the paradigm and practices of that Syndicate so we can see if he is not too distant from Hermetic beliefs. But right awat I can tell you that by being a Technocrat he is not going to believe in magick, he surely don\u2019t believe in the power of Will, nor consciousness nor anything like that. His paradigm is probably completely different from a mystic. So, in this case he do not fit. Maaaaybe, if he changes a little bit (scpecially from Science! To magick) he could fit the Fortunae.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (And no, I don't think there's much reason to think mages get to skip steps. For your example of a Disciple with many Sphere dots, absolutely not - a Hermetic of that rank is <i>expected to train apprentices. </i>The Order of Hermes thinks other Traditions <i>do magic wrong. </i>They're not going to leave the task of teaching the next generation of Hermetics to someone who, by their measure, dropped out of high school.) </div> </div> </div>Not all Hermetics train apprentices, even less in some of their 3 schools. So, the character is not going to be a teacher, unless he just decides to take a personal apprentice to teach his ways of magick.<br /> I\u2019d say that only a fraction of new Hermetics goes to formal training in a hermetic school. There are many that just learn directly from a mentor and others that just join the Tradition already awaken.<br /> Some Houses (and mentors) might be stricter about the training: I can see a Bonisagus wanting to teach more about complex rituals, or a Tytalus wanting to put the mage to the training from the beginning, but Flambeaus aren\u2019t worried like that. If the mage share the core traits of the Tradition and wants to explode Technocrats he will be welcomed into the House. Trad book also says that they are very open to new methods of magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sort of \u2013 </div> </div> </div>Ok, then if you want a Hermetic Martial Artist you need to have 4 practices. And if you want him to go Martial Arts and Yoga, then you need to pick 5 practices. Because, according to you, those 3 (HR,Dominion,Alchemy) are taught in training and absolutely no Hermetic can skip that training.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Consider how Hermetic mages who use technology apply their prior ritual knowledge to hypertech Practices or paradigms like &amp;quot;Everything is Data&amp;quot;. Verditus mages don't mean the same thing as Virtual Adepts do when they talk about &amp;quot;information.&amp;quot; Each Tradition has a culture, that's the point of the section of the Book of Secrets I highlighted. </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say that with few minor tweaks they could exchange Traditions. You just need to adapt the Science/magick thing. Even the box in OotH Trad book about the House Thig guy breaking into the vampire house is pretty similar to an Etherite and he would probably fit the Etherites. You see Traditions harshly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really important. </div> </div> </div>So the very core of Hermetic belief is not important? I don\u2019t know about other Traditions, we are talking about Hermetics. Again, all the books put too much emphasis in their foundations:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> M20:<br /> \u201cThis age\u2019s Hermetics are rolling up their sleeves and remaking the Order from its foundations while keping those foundations \u2013 confidence,knowledge,excellence, and Will \u2013 intact.\u201d<br /> Trad. Book:<br /> The essence of Hermetic belief comes down to a single concept: the ascendancy of the Will. The Order of Hermes believes that the power to shape reality stems solely from the wellsprings of Awakened human consciousness and the resolve to enforce the dictates of that consciousness. </div> </div> </div>If the Hermetic that is going to put someone into the Order thinks that the guy share those concepts, he wouldn\u2019t care about magia or kids training. That\u2019s for Sleepers who don\u2019t understand anything about magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Okay, this is something I can talk about more clearly.<br /> (\u2026) </div> </div> </div>To answer the questions first: He can\u2019t quite describe the energy scientifically. He can\u2019t put it in an equation, like sleeper known energy. That\u2019s why he has this mystical way of viewing it. <br /> The energy changes the world by serving as fuel to the consciousness of the mage. The origin of the energy is unknown to him, but probably related with the origin of the universe. It does not comes from the brain nor depends of humans to exist, though only humans can access it.<br /> To become invisible he can direct that energy in a way that light bends around the mage, just like a magnetic field bends iron particles. To read someone\u2019s memory he could <br /> He believes in all sort of umbrood, but he does not give them religious meaning. He may call them spirits, aliens, dimensional beings, whatever. He only knows that they are not from Earth. <br /> Quintessence is the very fabric of the universe and is, in fact, the energy that he taps into (maybe in another form) to cast his spells. Chaos Magick helps to focus it because it is directly related to human consciousness (though not created by it) and Chaos Magick is a practice that deals directly with belief, which is part of that consciousness.<br /> I appreciate your help in those examples. <br /> Sven is very close to what I want, excpt for some details: the field is not generated by human minds. Also, he doesn\u2019t use energy, which is one of the main instruments of the char and my char do believe machines can be used to tap into that energy. Other than that he fits. As I said, my char can easily be an Etherite. I\u2019m just reluctant because he will lose the \u201cmage\u201d flavour and not going to cast \u201cspells\u201d. Also, as you said he is not a great Scientist.<br /> Fiona has scientific background, but she has almost none of my char instruments. Other than alchemy and believing in angels she is pretty similar to my char. But she put few importance to energy (core of my char). What i think is that those aspects where they differ are not that primordial as their mindset.<br /> <br /> What I really wanted was a char that is all sleeper science, including to explain some effects, but threat magick as magick, unknown to science, arcane knowledge and has a &quot;mage&quot; and &quot;spell&quot; flavour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T07:43:50-08:00","id":1351038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351015#post1351015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice examples.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -Wait, let's not forget that he has &amp;quot;machines&amp;quot; as Instrument, I'm sure we can work with that: Albeit he's too lazzy to tell us *how* do they work to enhance his Will (or to manipulate the Force?), I'm sure we can squeeze a theory that's more than repeating the word Will over and over...<br /> <br /> ...if only because machines have to *do* something mechanical or physical that &amp;quot;works&amp;quot; on that Will/counsciousness (or on the Force?) somehow, and properly explaining *that* undoubtedly requires more than one single syllable, and perhaps some &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; words like brain, nervous system, psychosomatic, or a formula to explain how mechanisms and mundane energies could relate to the Force. Maybe even the word Ether, that we like so much<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Like Etherites?<br /> <br /> Don't make things harder than they are. For most Etherite characters, saying the word &amp;quot;Ether&amp;quot; suffices to explain most things (the classic Ether Goggles come to mind. You can use them as Instrument to see anything, why?, because Ether). If you're altering the etheric waveform with your honed psionic powers, that's something Etherites can understand.<br /> <br /> Other Etherites aren't going to complain because your theory isn't solid or scientific enough, Etherites may think your Science! it's <i>boring, </i>and doesn't deserve the apostrophe, because it's too all encompassing and leaves little space for maths and actual engineering.<br /> <br /> ...but, on the other hand: As Five Eyes points out, Hermetics will refuse to grant you the title of &amp;quot;<i>mage</i>&amp;quot;, you're to be treated like an apprentice until you learn ALL of their curriculum, the wizardly symbolisms that your character dislikes (even if you refuse to use them as Instrument). And you're not going to be popular there either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Etherite can fit, but won't be well received there nor would had the &quot;mage&quot; aspect.<br /> As I posted I wanted a &quot;mage&quot; with heavy sleeper science influence . <br /> <br /> About the Order, I believe that I made a good case in my last post. Please feel free to opine and answer too. For your post I only say ask: do you really believe that Hermetics char are limited to those 3 practices or having 5-6 (which is not good)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T10:40:27-08:00","id":1351065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351038#post1351038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the Order, I believe that I made a good case in my last post. Please feel free to opine and answer too. For your post I only say ask: do you really believe that Hermetics char are limited to those 3 practices or having 5-6 (which is not good)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody said that the mage has to chose those practices as Practices, but rather that the mage needs to know them and embed them in his own Practice/s in order to feel like a Hermetic (and to be better accepted in the Tradition).<br /> <br /> This is better represented in the mechanics by having Esoterica(Hermeticism), and thinking how to apply the esoterical theory to the Martial Arts form or Psionics, or whatever Practice you choose. IOC, rather than an Ether field, you could tap into a rich Imaginal World created by the minds of humans (like Chaos Mages do) or by the Divine (like traditional Hermetics do), for instance.<br /> <br /> You're embroiled in <b>meaningless</b> terminology that doersn't help to get the &quot;spirit&quot; of the mage. Those words you're using: Will, Practice, Energy...mean nothing without a context. It's better to not use &quot;code words&quot; to define a mage's &quot;aspect&quot; unless it's needed to clarify, instead use words as your mage would.<br /> <br /> For instance: you talk about &quot;Machines&quot;. What kind of machines, how do they look and why/how your mage believes they work?. Just saying &quot;I'm going to use machines&quot; doesn't help to imagine what you're going to do at all (as machines it's a rather ample category).<br /> <br /> You need to similarly describe each element of the Focus. A mystical Foucs describes a Reality ruled by magic and the supernatural, where every action it's magical, a scientific Focus described a reality with paranormal phenomena that can be known trough reason and theory, a Mystic Scientist sits somewhere in the middle...this can't be easily escaped<br /> <br /> To give you an example of how your Focus application it's &quot;broader than you think&quot;: Your Paradigm almost certainly will influence what your character thinks about <i>science</i>. While the main function of the Paradigm it's to explain why magick works, more often than not it's<i> a huge declaration about the universe as a whole</i> ... and that will include science. If Everything is Chaos, then lowercase science (as part of everything) it's fundamentally wrong in some very core aspects (namely, thinking that there's such thing as universal laws to be discovered)<br /> <br /> This cosmovision it's all very important to see where your mage fits...just saying Will it's not enough to convince anyone here because while it IS important for the Hermetics, you have lots of pages *qualifying* what &quot;Will&quot; <i>means </i>for them. Where you're now, Will and &quot;psychic powers&quot; sounds like they're the one and the same for your char...that's not very Hermetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-26-2019, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T16:24:36-08:00","id":1351152,"title":"","content":"Magical fellowships have overarching values, within which each mage expresses their individual paradigm. Revised called this the Tradition's &quot;paradigm&quot;, and M20 calls it a &quot;preferred Focus&quot; (see the Book of Secrets), just as the term is used for the individual paradigm/Focus of mages within the fellowship. The Order of Hermes is one of the most rigid Traditions in terms of training, though its Focus is highly flexible <i>once you're established. </i>The House Xaos mages are allowed to practice their iconoclastic magic because they &quot;talk the talk&quot; and can discuss chaos magick through the lens of proper Hermetic training. (Other Traditions, such as the Akashics and Euthanatos, have more strident requirements - both of those groups have a fundamental code which initiates must affirm. Sort of like converting to a religion.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351037#post1351037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One more point, you think in a time of need like the Ascension war, the Order would dump a good, intelligent, determined, Willed mage because of some minor differences or lack of formal training?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. he seems like he might be an ideal candidate. You know how you fix someone with wrong ideas and a lack of training? You <b><i>train </i></b>him.<br /> <br /> Hey, Satyros Brucato, remind me how the Order of Hermes trains mages again?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>M20,pg149</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">these consummate scholars master ancient and arcane rituals through constant study and intense practice. Tapping elemental currents through<br /> incantations, signs, seals, paraphernalia, and secret languages, the Hermetics are \u2013 by necessity \u2013 secretive and suspicious. They command tremendous power, after all, and<br /> their rivals lurk everywhere. Alchemy, dominion, and High Ritual form core practices within the Order\u2019s ranks. No Hermetic mage lacks such training. </div> </div> </div> </div>The M20 Book of Secrets re-emphasizes the rigid order in which Hermetics are taught magickal techniques. I can't think of a single scrap of evidence suggesting an untrained mage will be welcomed to the Order as a full member just because he said the magick word (&quot;Will&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351037#post1351037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all Hermetics train apprentices, even less in some of their 3 schools. So, the character is not going to be a teacher, unless he just decides to take a personal apprentice to teach his ways of magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hermetics of 5th degree or higher are <i>required </i>to train apprentices. It's part of the Code of Hermes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351037#post1351037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, then if you want a Hermetic Martial Artist you need to have 4 practices. And if you want him to go Martial Arts and Yoga, then you need to pick 5 practices. Because, according to you, those 3 (HR,Dominion,Alchemy) are taught in training and absolutely no Hermetic can skip that training.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to me and, y'know, the books.<br /> <br /> Having training in a practice doesn't mean it's one of your chosen Practices. Most every real-world chaos magician studied Levi-esque high ritual first. In fact it'd be hard to make sense of the practice of chaos magick without prior training elsewhere, as it's an eclectic &quot;digested&quot; practice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351037#post1351037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the very core of Hermetic belief is not important? I don\u2019t know about other Traditions, we are talking about Hermetics. Again, all the books put too much emphasis in their foundations:</div> </div> </div> </div>White noise at this point, really. As I said, Hermetic training is about realizing and mastering your Will (and Word) and learning how to make it work. Someone without training doesn't know their own Will (or, as I have provided evidence for, isn't even using their Will according to the Order.) You don't let them skip the fundamentals.<br /> <br /> You're proposing that someone who &quot;believes in Jesus&quot; should be ordained as a priest without attending seminary because he accepts the &quot;very core&quot; of Christian beliefs.<br /> <br /> Is Scientist Sven a suitable Hermetic? He thinks the power to change reality is the sole province of humanity and that his effects come from within, and shares a Practice (Chaos magick.)<br /> Is every mage with a &quot;World of Chaos&quot; Paradigma suitable Hermetic? They necessarily believe the power to shape reality comes from themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351037#post1351037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To become invisible he can direct that energy in a way that light bends around the mage, just like a magnetic field bends iron particles. To read someone\u2019s memory he could</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of cut off there?<br /> <br /> To clarify, is the order of operations:<br /> <br /> 1.) The world is the product of Consciousness. A separate energy permeates this place, but it's not created by Consciousness - it just helps fuel it. Through various Instruments, it is possible to draw some of that energy into yourself, which allows your Consciousness to make changes to the world. (This is akin to Scientist Sven's view, and fits how you describe it as a &quot;fuel&quot;.)<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> 2.) The world is permeated by an Energy. Through various instruments, it is possible to elevate your Consciousness to such a point that it can direct the energy, which changes the world. (This is akin to Fiona's view, and fits the statement that you can &quot;direct the energy in a way that bends light.&quot;)<br /> <br /> What does this guy think Ascension is? Does he believe in it at all? Why can't Sleepers do magick, in this guy's estimation? What's an Avatar?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351037#post1351037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I really wanted was a char that is all sleeper science, including to explain some effects, but threat magick as magick, unknown to science, arcane knowledge and has a &quot;mage&quot; and &quot;spell&quot; flavour.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do &quot;mage&quot; and &quot;spell&quot; flavors mean, if the character is consciously avoiding occult principles and mystic practices in favor of abstract, ad hoc, or scientific ones? Like if you want things which feel like spells, why doesn't this guy use incantations and wands?<br /> <br /> Mages like Fiona can describe their effects in scientific terms, but rely on mystical causes (which they'd just say are undiscovered scientific causes). Most Hermetics from a science background can discuss how, say, the astrological influence of Mars can excite atoms to create heat, though they may consider that Sleeper physics knowledge to be basically secondary to the deeper occult lore.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't feel like what you're aiming at, which seems to be more of a &quot;character who is a mystic but who has no spiritual or mystical beliefs&quot;. We spend more time talking about the things the character <i>doesn't </i>believe in than what they <i>do, </i>and often those seem to be purely descriptive - he believes what he's doing is magic instead of science, but why does he think that? Why does his drive to reconcile things with his scientific background pump the brakes when it comes to describing what &quot;the energy&quot; is or how &quot;consciousness&quot; works?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T18:18:13-08:00","id":1351189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351152#post1351152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all. he seems like he might be an ideal candidate. You know how you fix someone with wrong ideas and a lack of training? You <b><i>train </i></b>him.<br /> <br /> Hey, Satyros Brucato, remind me how the Order of Hermes trains mages again?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The M20 Book of Secrets re-emphasizes the rigid order in which Hermetics are taught magickal techniques. I can't think of a single scrap of evidence suggesting an untrained mage will be welcomed to the Order as a full member just because he said the magick word (&quot;Will&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with you in the case of the Syndicate you posted. He is a great candidate, but his beliefs are completely opposite of what a mage (moreso Hermetic) believe. He would indeed need some tweaks from his master. Now I also agree that my char would also need some (even minors) tweaks, since he do share some traits.<br /> I'd say he would learn Hermetic history, laws, rules and possibly some magickal concepts like getting a Word. But go into full training? Aboslutely not. He doesn't even <b>can</b> train like an new apprentice since he's already awakened and goetia/theurgia is sleeper sorcery. <br /> The max they can do is <b>try</b> to mold his already stablished belief into their own, which doesn't mean teaching new practices, but trying to put some of their beliefs into the char's ones. Now, I don't know what would be the result of that..<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hermetics of 5th degree or higher are <i>required </i>to train apprentices. It's part of the Code of Hermes. </div> </div> </div>No they do not. It is desirable for them, though, because this helps to increase influency inside the Order and is good to have someone at your side doing &quot;favors&quot; for you. It is even said that some Hermetics go without students because older and more powerful members take precedence.<br /> That is not even a problem, though, if a Hermetic do not want to train anybody, he jus won't. And if he was obligated to do (which isn't) he would just train with the focus he wants. He's the teacher afterall.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> According to me and, y'know, the books.<br /> <br /> Having training in a practice doesn't mean it's one of your chosen Practices. Most every real-world chaos magician studied Levi-esque high ritual first. In fact it'd be hard to make sense of the practice of chaos magick without prior training elsewhere, as it's an eclectic &quot;digested&quot; practice. </div> </div> </div>By your logic, my mage could just learn all they have to teach and throw it all away and continue to use magick as he knows it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> White noise at this point, really. As I said, Hermetic training is about realizing and mastering your Will (and Word) and learning how to make it work. Someone without training doesn't know their own Will (or, as I have provided evidence for, isn't even using their Will according to the Order.) You don't let them skip the fundamentals.<br /> <br /> You're proposing that someone who &quot;believes in Jesus&quot; should be ordained as a priest without attending seminary because he accepts the &quot;very core&quot; of Christian beliefs.<br /> <br /> Is Scientist Sven a suitable Hermetic? He thinks the power to change reality is the sole province of humanity and that his effects come from within, and shares a Practice (Chaos magick.)<br /> Is every mage with a &quot;World of Chaos&quot; Paradigma suitable Hermetic? They necessarily believe the power to shape reality comes from themselves. </div> </div> </div>What if the Order thinks the mage is using Will as they do? Why are you saying that those &quot;Wills&quot; are different? Just because of different practices and the lack of High Ritual training? Will is not realted to any of them. What is the difference between the Order Will and the Will stated many times in M20?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sort of cut off there?<br /> <br /> To clarify, is the order of operations:<br /> <br /> 1.) The world is the product of Consciousness. A separate energy permeates this place, but it's not created by Consciousness - it just helps fuel it. Through various Instruments, it is possible to draw some of that energy into yourself, which allows your Consciousness to make changes to the world. (This is akin to Scientist Sven's view, and fits how you describe it as a &quot;fuel&quot;.) </div> </div> </div>You mean as if Consciousness created the world and universe? If that's the case, then no. Consciousness just let's you change the unverse and my mage does that by using that energy (that also isn't created by consciousness).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> OR<br /> <br /> 2.) The world is permeated by an Energy. Through various instruments, it is possible to elevate your Consciousness to such a point that it can direct the energy, which changes the world. (This is akin to Fiona's view, and fits the statement that you can &quot;direct the energy in a way that bends light.&quot;) </div> </div> </div>This seems more fiting, yes. To resume, the universe was created (no one knows how) and with that creation came the energy that is everywhere. to make changes, he uses that energy that is in fact helping the Consciousness shape Reality. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does this guy think Ascension is? Does he believe in it at all? Why can't Sleepers do magick, in this guy's estimation? What's an Avatar? </div> </div> </div>Good questions. He probably think Ascension is completely merging your Consciousness with the Universe, whatever that means. He probably do not have much defined opinion other than that. Sleepers can't do magick because they cannot use their Consciousness in a way that changes Reality. About the Avatar, he would probably believe they are an personification of the energy that guides you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What do &quot;mage&quot; and &quot;spell&quot; flavors mean, if the character is consciously avoiding occult principles and mystic practices in favor of abstract, ad hoc, or scientific ones? Like if you want things which feel like spells, why doesn't this guy use incantations and wands? </div> </div> </div><br /> Mages like Fiona can describe their effects in scientific terms, but rely on mystical causes (which they'd just say are undiscovered scientific causes). Most Hermetics from a science background can discuss how, say, the astrological influence of Mars can excite atoms to create heat, though they may consider that Sleeper physics knowledge to be basically secondary to the deeper occult lore.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't feel like what you're aiming at, which seems to be more of a &quot;character who is a mystic but who has no spiritual or mystical beliefs&quot;. We spend more time talking about the things the character <i>doesn't </i>believe in than what they <i>do, </i>and often those seem to be purely descriptive - he believes what he's doing is magic instead of science, but why does he think that? Why does his drive to reconcile things with his scientific background pump the brakes when it comes to describing what &quot;the energy&quot; is or how &quot;consciousness&quot; works?[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Because spells can be done in many other ways. He just uses the ones that he discovered/trained. I'm answering Aleph in my next post and I'm going to describe more about the char.<br /> <br /> About the &quot;mage&quot; and &quot;spell&quot; flavor: to me, using and unknown (arcane) energy that has no direct explanation to how the effect works feels like a spell. Its's like the effect is mystic until you reach the instrument. Then it is more scientific. He can't explain exactly (equations,etc.)how the energy works. He definitely has no religious nor symbolism belief. But I'd say it is mystical because of the unknown nature of it.<br /> <br /> Having a &quot;mage&quot; flavor means that he won't explain with things like &quot;Oh, I'm just using my brain wave pattern to ressonate into the right frequeny of the energy&quot;. That's a Scientist flavor. He pumps the brake because he just can't explain his paradigm like that. His conciliation of scientific background is just to show the way he study magick (experiments,etc.) and to explain the very end of the effects (bending light to get invisible, altering electric potential to create lightning, etc.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T18:19:10-08:00","id":1351190,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's why I said 5-6 practices, being 3 of them HR,Alchemy and Dominion and the others the ones the character will really use. That makes no sense. Mage is a very limitless game, limiting a char this way seems wrong to me.<br /> He would definitely have Esoterica, probably with (body control).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351065#post1351065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're embroiled in <b>meaningless</b> terminology that doersn't help to get the &quot;spirit&quot; of the mage. Those words you're using: Will, Practice, Energy...mean nothing without a context. It's better to not use &quot;code words&quot; to define a mage's &quot;aspect&quot; unless it's needed to clarify, instead use words as your mage would.<br /> <br /> For instance: you talk about &quot;Machines&quot;. What kind of machines, how do they look and why/how your mage believes they work?. Just saying &quot;I'm going to use machines&quot; doesn't help to imagine what you're going to do at all (as machines it's a rather ample category).<br /> <br /> You need to similarly describe each element of the Focus. A mystical Foucs describes a Reality ruled by magic and the supernatural, where every action it's magical, a scientific Focus described a reality with paranormal phenomena that can be known trough reason and theory, a Mystic Scientist sits somewhere in the middle...this can't be easily escaped<br /> <br /> To give you an example of how your Focus application it's &quot;broader than you think&quot;: Your Paradigm almost certainly will influence what your character thinks about <i>science</i>. While the main function of the Paradigm it's to explain why magick works, more often than not it's<i> a huge declaration about the universe as a whole</i> ... and that will include science. If Everything is Chaos, then lowercase science (as part of everything) it's fundamentally wrong in some very core aspects (namely, thinking that there's such thing as universal laws to be discovered)<br /> <br /> This cosmovision it's all very important to see where your mage fits...just saying Will it's not enough to convince anyone here because while it IS important for the Hermetics, you have lots of pages *qualifying* what &quot;Will&quot; <i>means </i>for them. Where you're now, Will and &quot;psychic powers&quot; sounds like they're the one and the same for your char...that's not very Hermetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I could describe it even more. And I disagree about the meaningless terminology (they are used often in the books), but I'll try to do it without them.<br /> <br /> Indeed, there are like 3 instruments that I chose that were not very well described and could be enhanced to fit better an Hermetic paradigm. I don't want, though, to change any of the focus (paradigm/prcatices/instrument), nor add religion to it.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Paradigm</u></b>: &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot;, &quot;Consciousness is the one true reality&quot;, &quot;Might is rigth&quot;.<br /> <br /> After awakening through intense study from esoteric sources, he began to understand that the universe is more than the physical matter/energy we know today. It is greatly influenced by the conscioussness of all living beings. Part of the meaning of life itself is to give a meaning to the universe and change it, mold it with the power of life very own conscioussness. This means that your belief is capacble of molding reality and that the ones with a stronger mind/belief is going to be in the upper tier of the world.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Practices</u></b>: &quot;Chaos Magick&quot;, &quot;Martial Arts&quot;, &quot;Psionics&quot;<br /> <br /> He discovered that the universe and all that's inside it is made of a special kind of arcane energy (Quintesence) that can be interacted in a metaphysical level. This energy seems to be everywhere and everything is made (or comes from) it. The practices he has is just a way to direct/influence this energy in the manner that the result that he wants happen.Just like a painter wanting to change what's in his frame uses a brush, so the mage uses his practice to alter the world as he so desires.<br /> Chaos Magick is the Art of shaping reality according to the mage's belief. It is about raising and directing that energy in any way the mage believe that works.<br /> Being violent,determined and a enthusiast of the body, Martial Arts and bodybuilding were always part of his life. In this way it is natural for him to change his state of mind (Psionics) to tap into that energy.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Instruments</u></b>: Energy,Gestures, Meditation, Eye Contact, Weapons, Books/Scrolls/Periodics, Devices/Machines<br /> <br /> <b>Energy</b>: This is the core of the character focus. Pratically everything he does is involving energy, that are the brush swabed by his Awakened conscioussness. It will be present in almost all his effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Gestures/Meditation</b>: Those are deeply connected to his Martial Arts training and Psionics development, they are a way of directing the energy with the power of his body and Awakened mind. Effects like conjuring electric arcs (Gestures) or improving his body features (Meditation) are made this way.<br /> <br /> <b>Eye Contact</b>: With intensive training and experimentation he learned how to &quot;see&quot; different patterns in that energy, be in living beings or not. Sensing effects, like scaning a body for deseases are done this way.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons</b>: In the midle of combat, his mind and body become one with his weapons. He handle his weapons in a natural way, as if being guided to his targets. Combat effects are done this way.<br /> <br /> <b>Books/Scrolls/Periodics</b>: Knowledge is power and books is all about knowledge. He likes to study both sleeper science and magickal theory. Magickal theory is how magick behaves, how Paradox and Quintessence works, what and how Consensus works, etc. By studying or simply reading a book or scroll, being it a engineering book or a arcane tome, he can achieve the state of mind necessary to change Reality. All kinds of effects can be achieved through this technique, you only need the right book/periodic to direct your conscioussness into that way. Often used to conjure powerful rituals that demand more time to cast. (<u>This is the instrument I had the less ideas and would love to see more examples or ideas to use it.</u>).<br /> <br /> <b>Devices/Machines</b>: One of his first instruments used to tap the energy. At first he used simple yet efficient devices like coils, receivers, modulators to raise and diret the energy the way he wanted. With time, he understood that he was affecting the machines output by himself and they were mere instruments to help him in this. He began using more rudimentary devices, involving crystals coupled with wires in their interior to gather the energy. He began using them less and less to the point that eventually he stopped using them altogether (dropped instrument). It is important to note that this was an initial stage, he didn't relied on them for long and they was very, very rudimentar and simple. He didn't quite understood yet the mysteries of the energy and was trying to use science and technology to get a result. When he realised the mystical aspect that that energy had, he stopped trying to explain it that way. I'd say that all kind of effects could be done this way, it is just a matter of using the right device in the right way. After dropping this instrument, he might use them more like a totem of his Awakened Will than a device per se.<br /> <br /> So, I guess this is explained enough. I would love to see your opinions about it and am willing to makes changes. But I wouldn't like to change the focus list.<br /> <br /> Now, why would the Order of Hermes be intersted on him?<br /> He is an aggressive, determined <b>mage</b>. He probably awoke by himself and began his mage life as an Orphan, later joining the Order. He share the Order's foundations and some beliefs, he is definitely a Traditional and is bold, cocky, power/knowledge-hungry House Flambeau would be the place for him. He has heavy knowledge of the forces of nature and is very fond of electricity (and vulgar magick). He would be seen as a very great weapon in the war against Technocracy, even that he doesn't completely fit the Order stereotype.<br /> <br /> And why would the Etherites want him?<br /> He is an engineer and has a scientifical mind. He is always seeking knowledge and is very dedicated. That is enough for them to have him there, even that only to learn more with him. Many would see him as a farse, or even a joke because of his beliefs. Calling himself a mage and believeing that everything the Tradition do is magick do not help his case. While he might fit this Tradition, that's not the feel I want to this char...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 11-26-2019, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-26T19:47:26-08:00","id":1351205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351189#post1351189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say he would learn Hermetic history, laws, rules and possibly some magickal concepts like getting a Word. But go into full training? Aboslutely not. He doesn't even <b>can</b> train like an new apprentice since he's already awakened and goetia/theurgia is sleeper sorcery. The max they can do is <b>try</b> to mold his already stablished belief into their own, which doesn't mean teaching new practices, but trying to put some of their beliefs into the char's ones. Now, I don't know what would be the result of that..</div> </div> </div> </div>An Initiate (a full mage of the Order) doesn't receive training - they've graduated. Apprentices do, and the Order has a strict and rigorous curriculum for them. It's true you can't make a Mage &quot;go backwards&quot;, but the extended summary of apprenticeship in their original Tradbook presumes Awakened apprentices go through the same steps - they undergo the same training, in rigid order, as anyone else, but are presumably achieving their magical effects through dynamic magic instead of static. M20 again refers to this strict order, and it's reiterated in their RevTradbook - I can't see any evidence to think it's no longer canonical. An Awakened apprentice <i>might </i>be awarded Practicus status ahead of the curve, but I see no reason to think the Order - with its ancient curriculum and emphasis on doing things the right way - would rush someone's training just because they're talented. (Quite possibly the opposite - it's doubly important to make sure a talented student doesn't get rushed into a role they're not ready for.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351189#post1351189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No they do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Code of Hermes is in their Tradbook. The relevant section is on page 45. Fifth Degree initiates are on the list, and are passed up by the demands of their senior mages. They are responsible for the apprentice, so if they debut an ill-trained lout whose training shames the Order, they themselves will presumably face the punishment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351189#post1351189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By your logic, my mage could just learn all they have to teach and throw it all away and continue to use magick as he knows it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, he could be an apostate who renounces all he learned - but at that point, why was the character ever a Hermetic?<br /> <br /> I feel you're being inflexible on the idea that Practices are distinct things that you use or don't use. A Hermetic Tytalan wrestler whose Practices are Martial Arts, Dominion, and Yoga is still a participant in the Order's educational system and philosophy. His Focus as a whole would reflect its heavy focus on occult rules and arcane correspondences. He'd have a more ritualistic or alchemical approach to physical exercise than, say, an Akashic or Syndicate wrestler.<br /> <br /> Do you agree that a Dreamspeaker whose Paradigm is Might is Right and who uses Martial Arts and Dominion as their Focus is not the same as a Hermetic with the same Paradigm and Practices? Even if, say, their Instruments are identical? What if we replace the Dreamspeaker with an Akashic? Why is this the case, if these are all mystics? Is the only difference really just &quot;one of them says Will and the other one says Do&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351189#post1351189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Order thinks the mage is using Will as they do? Why are you saying that those &quot;Wills&quot; are different? Just because of different practices and the lack of High Ritual training? Will is not realted to any of them. What is the difference between the Order Will and the Will stated many times in M20?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Order believes Will is focused, deliberate, energetic, personal, and forceful, the product of pursuing your Word and self-realization through Hermetic cultivation. You use Will not to seek the favor of deities or harness occult forces but to command them. It requires &quot;resolve&quot; to enforce its &quot;dictates.&quot; It's something their training strives to &quot;build&quot; - a lifelong project of finding out exactly who you are. That's why I don't think a raw recruit's claim to Will would be taken seriously - Hermetic Will is something you <i>discover</i> through Hermetic study.<br /> <br /> This doesn't have anything to do with High Ritual or with any particular Practice (though this is why Dominion is one of their core Practices.) Rather, this is what M20 would call the Orders' &quot;preferred Focus&quot;. The Order's egocentric small-p paradigms and practices lead them to egocentric Paradigms and Practices. &quot;<i>My </i>Will be Done&quot; and not &quot;Thy Will Be Done&quot;.<br /> <br /> Compare this to the unfocused, haphazard, contemplative, impersonal, or receptive Will-working of any number of Traditions, Crafts, and Conventions. If the Hermetics are right about what Will is, every other mage is somehow using magick without using Will. The Order of Hermes realized correctly that the true source of magick is <i>within</i>, but this doesn't mean their paradigm (or preferred Focus, in M20) is the objectively correct one - it understands the &quot;inside&quot; and &quot;outside&quot; in Hermetic terms, and it has accumulated some preconceptions on what the correct way to do magick is - and therefore, what Will is. You've mentioned a lack of familiarity with the other Traditions - that's a shame! Having a more complete picture would help bring these distinctions into focus.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the long-form exploration of your character. I'll take a look at it and let you know if I come up with anything I think would be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 11-27-2019, 05:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T02:49:11-08:00","id":1351247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351190#post1351190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I guess this is explained enough. I would love to see your opinions about it and am willing to makes changes. But I wouldn't like to change the focus list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose my first instinct is to wonder what Chaos magic is doing on the list of Practices - it doesn't seem to be reflected in any of the chosen Instruments, and I don't see any of the signatures of the Practice in the character's methods. Much of Chaos Magic is symbol-driven, using ad hoc systems of occult symbolism or archetypical forms to focus the mind on a desired outcome - but I'm not sure why we'd have a character who rejects symbolic approaches adopt a Practice where you're expected to use tons of them. Is there some Instrument the character uses where they fixate on or meditate towards a desired outcome to bring it about, law of attraction style? Or do they meditate on mental exemplars to embody them? Another branch of chaos magic is socially performative, but I'd expect to see that paired with another Practice (most often dominion or Ars Cupid), and it doesn't seem like this guy's style to use social abstractions...<br /> <br /> It still feels odd for the character to resist proposing a scientific theory of what the energy is and how he interacts with it - we're to understand he's extremely intellectually curious and not prone to superstition or symbolism, yet the most important energy in his life - one which governs the entire universe, and which he can register on mechanical instruments for measurement - is not subjected to scientific scrutiny, but is instead accepted as numinous and otherworldly?<br /> <br /> The Books/Scrolls Instrument runs into something I've always been skeptical of when it shows up at my table - an extremely broadly applicable instrument with a very abstract, Purple mechanism. How does this Instrument interact with the energy to bring about some change? The character's other instruments are immediately practical means of directing and measuring the energy, this one is the only case where they seem to deal in abstractions.<br /> <br /> Beyond those hiccups, I think you've got a fairly normal psionic Orphan. He doesn't really have the scientific curiosity typical of an Etherite, given his shrug-and-move-on approach to metaphysics. This is someone very bright and dedicated who I suspect the Order of Hermes would love to get a chance to train, but Hermetics don't really have anything to offer the character as presented - if he doesn't buy into their philosophy or adopt any of their common Practices, the lack of overlap in instruments means their occult knowledge is all basically bunk to him, right? He's got no reason to give a shit what the Fifth Pentacle of Seven Moons does or how some long-dead Bonisagus describes Quintessence in Platonic terms, and he's not going to adopt ritualized chaos magick like harmonizing with thought-form deities or meditating on/towards symbolic representations of his personal problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T07:13:26-08:00","id":1351281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351205#post1351205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An Initiate (a full mage of the Order) doesn't receive training - they've graduated. Apprentices do, and the Order has a strict and rigorous curriculum for them. It's true you can't make a Mage &amp;quot;go backwards&amp;quot;, but the extended summary of apprenticeship in their original Tradbook presumes Awakened apprentices go through the same steps - they undergo the same training, in rigid order, as anyone else, but are presumably achieving their magical effects through dynamic magic instead of static. M20 again refers to this strict order, and it's reiterated in their RevTradbook - I can't see any evidence to think it's no longer canonical. An Awakened apprentice <i>might </i>be awarded Practicus status ahead of the curve, but I see no reason to think the Order - with its ancient curriculum and emphasis on doing things the right way - would rush someone's training just because they're talented. (Quite possibly the opposite - it's doubly important to make sure a talented student doesn't get rushed into a role they're not ready for.)</div> </div> </div> </div>We are not talking about a talented student. It's a fully Awakened mage. He is not going to learn goetia and theurgy anymore (it's not possible nor needed). <br /> The books have no words on already Awakened mage entering the Order. I'm pretty sure he might get some training in linguistics, history of the Order and the Code of Hermes, as well as getting a Word and True Name. But I don't believe he would go through all the training as if were a sleeper.<br /> Imagine a Chorister with Arete 4, and several Shperes with 3-4 dots that joins the Order for whatever reason. They might teach the basics as I posted, but they would not put a rank 5(2 dots in a Sphere) to train a guy like that. Hell, it would be an insult to try to teach such a powerful mage anything related to magick.<br /> <br /> Another point is that there are only 3 Hermetic schools. Certainly not all new Hermetic (Sleeper or not) have the chance of going to one. So, the training might be made directly from another Hermetic, which means his own practices, if a little different frombthe Order standard, will influence the apprentice. <br /> I think we have discussed that enough and we'll have to agree to disagree. Unless you bring concret evidence that even a fully grown ass Master that join the Order has to pass everything a Sleeper pass, I think we're have to stay with our personal opinions. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, he could be an apostate who renounces all he learned - but at that point, why was the character ever a Hermetic? </div> </div> </div>Because those practices are the only thing I don't like too much in the Order. They are so much more than this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you agree that a Dreamspeaker whose Paradigm is Might is Right and who uses Martial Arts and Dominion as their Focus is not the same as a Hermetic with the same Paradigm and Practices? Even if, say, their Instruments are identical? What if we replace the Dreamspeaker with an Akashic? Why is this the case, if these are all mystics? Is the only difference really just &amp;quot;one of them says Will and the other one says Do&amp;quot;? </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not. In fact, every mage is different and believe in different things, even that they share the exact same focus.<br /> While they might have different beliefs they would cast spells pretty similarly, though.<br /> If their practices and instruments are the same, then they use the same techniques to cast spells even thst for different reasons (if they hsve different paradigms).<br /> Now, if they share all 3 (paradigm/practices /instruments) then only their personal take on them will differentiate, which includes their Traditions.<br /> So, for your example, if the Akashic and Hermetic shared all their focus, the Hermetic would use Martial Arts to reach a state of focus that let's him direct his True Will more efficiently, while the Akashic uses Martial Arts to elevate his spirit and transcend the material world to change Reality, for example.<br /> Externally they are doing the same things.<br /> All mages focus are different and that's why you might have an Hermetic that do notbuse symbols or religion. Rev trad book have examples of Hermetics that do not care for those details, like the Neighbour Friend and thst Livia girl, who were actually a Children of Knowledge and joined the Order (probably without going through sleeper training lvl).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Order believes Will is focused, deliberate, energetic, personal, and forceful, the product of pursuing your Word and self-realization through Hermetic cultivation. You use Will not to seek the favor of deities or harness occult forces but to command them. It requires &amp;quot;resolve&amp;quot; to enforce its &amp;quot;dictates.&amp;quot; It's something their training strives to &amp;quot;build&amp;quot; - a lifelong project of finding out exactly who you are. That's why I don't think a raw recruit's claim to Will would be taken seriously - Hermetic Will is something you <i>discover</i> through Hermetic study.<br /> <br /> This doesn't have anything to do with High Ritual or with any particular Practice (though this is why Dominion is one of their core Practices.) Rather, this is what M20 would call the Orders' &amp;quot;preferred Focus&amp;quot;. The Order's egocentric small-p paradigms and practices lead them to egocentric Paradigms and Practices. &amp;quot;<i>My </i>Will be Done&amp;quot; and not &amp;quot;Thy Will Be Done&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Compare this to the unfocused, haphazard, contemplative, impersonal, or receptive Will-working of any number of Traditions, Crafts, and Conventions. If the Hermetics are right about what Will is, every other mage is somehow using magick without using Will. The Order of Hermes realized correctly that the true source of magick is <i>within</i>, but this doesn't mean their paradigm (or preferred Focus, in M20) is the objectively correct one - it understands the &amp;quot;inside&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;outside&amp;quot; in Hermetic terms, and it has accumulated some preconceptions on what the correct way to do magick is - and therefore, what Will is. You've mentioned a lack of familiarity with the other Traditions - that's a shame! Having a more complete picture would help bring these distinctions into focus.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the long-form exploration of your character. I'll take a look at it and let you know if I come up with anything I think would be helpful. </div> </div> </div>I always saw Hermetic Will and any other mage Will as the same concept. The difference is thst tje Hermetics believe and state that they indeed are using their powerful Will, while other Traditions, while do cast magick using that same Will, do not acknowledge that. Is that the difference you're talking about? It is thr same Awakened Will but not acknowledge. <br /> Anyway, my mage definitely acknowledge thebuse of Will and do use it just as an Hermetic. Now, if your argument is that you somehow need to be trained by an Hermetic to use it this way, I'd love to know where did you get that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T07:44:52-08:00","id":1351283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351247#post1351247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose my first instinct is to wonder what Chaos magic is doing on the list of Practices - it doesn't seem to be reflected in any of the chosen Instruments, and I don't see any of the signatures of the Practice in the character's methods. Much of Chaos Magic is symbol-driven, using ad hoc systems of occult symbolism or archetypical forms to focus the mind on a desired outcome - but I'm not sure why we'd have a character who rejects symbolic approaches adopt a Practice where you're expected to use tons of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Chaos Magick is not symbolic, it is belief driven, so you might use symbolism or not. It include energy raising and directing and can accommodate almost any belief.<br /> So, it has energy, it has power in belief and is open enough. That's why I got it. Also, it is the glue that link the paradigm ro the instruments. The fact that consciousness (belief) afect reality using energy. Together with the other practices I think it fits. <br /> What you mean by not in any instrument and how would you change that? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there some Instrument the character uses where they fixate on or meditate towards a desired outcome to bring it about, law of attraction style? Or do they meditate on mental exemplars to embody them? </div> </div> </div>Law of atraction (As above, so bellow) is something I would see in this char. Meditation can be used with visualization that way, also the external instruments might work this way too (books, machines,weapons). Using them to fixate his mind and use visualization to the desired effect. This might work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It still feels odd for the character to resist proposing a scientific theory of what the energy is and how he interacts with it - we're to understand he's extremely intellectually curious and not prone to superstition or symbolism, yet the most important energy in his life - one which governs the entire universe, and which he can register on mechanical instruments for measurement - is not subjected to scientific scrutiny, but is instead accepted as numinous and otherworldly? </div> </div> </div>He do not resist. He just can't develop a scientific theory or equations to describe it. He also didn't measured it, his devices only could gather and direct it. He then decided to just study magick behavior instead of trying to mathematically map it. He treat it as apart from sleeper science because he believe science can't explain it properly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Books/Scrolls Instrument runs into something I've always been skeptical of when it shows up at my table - an extremely broadly applicable instrument with a very abstract, Purple mechanism. How does this Instrument interact with the energy to bring about some change? The character's other instruments are immediately practical means of directing and measuring the energy, this one is the only case where they seem to deal in abstractions. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Books is nore about Chaos Magick that works on a diferent Consciousness state snd belief.<br /> What would you suggest?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - if he doesn't buy into their philosophy or adopt any of their common Practices, the lack of overlap in instruments means their occult knowledge is all basically bunk to him, right? He's got no reason to give a shit what the Fifth Pentacle of Seven Moons does or how some long-dead Bonisagus describes Quintessence in Platonic terms, and he's not going to adopt ritualized chaos magick like harmonizing with thought-form deities or meditating on/towards symbolic representations of his personal problems. </div> </div> </div>I think you are being too specific. Not all Hermetics give this importance to symbolisms. Rev trad book has some examples. He share others beliefs, including the desire to learn the working of magick. <br /> I'd see him as a flashy Flambeau using his deep knowledge of science and electricity in his vulgar spells..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T00:50:57-08:00","id":1351427,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.<br /> <br /> As to your proposed Chorister convert - the Order has not, historically, been particularly hesitant to insult mages from other Traditions. Remember, &quot;<i>What mage in any rival Tradition, of whatever skill, can boast the comprehensive knowledge of our least Adept?</i>&quot; Do you think the Order believes a Dreamspeaker or Technocrat, &quot;of whatever skill&quot;, knows the first thing about how magick actually works? If a Chorister has been using inadequate magic - little better than the theurgia taught to apprentices - their entire life, don't you need to start from the basics before you can teach them how to do it right?<br /> <br /> Why is your example for &quot;non-traditional&quot; Hermetic approaches someone trained in another Tradition altogether and grandfathered in (and even then, she's still an Alchemist!)?<br /> Why is your example for non-symbolic, non-religious mages a guy who explicitly finds Hermetic ritualism comforting and compatible with his Catholic upbringing?<br /> These seem like odd choices?<br /> <br /> I hold Hermetic Will to be a subset of the Will exercised by all other mages. Compare their criteria for Will to that exercised by other mages - and remember, their criticism isn't that other mages refuse to acknowledge their own Will as the source of power. They say other mages are ill-trained, slavish blunderers - that they're technically, academically, and spiritually backwards. That they beg and plead and surrender their wills to forces outside of themselves. How can servility be Willful? And if it is Willful - then why would the Hermetics, who exult Will above all, sneer at it? If it works, it must be true Will, and yet the Order thinks otherwise. If they had a genuine understanding of what true Will was, why would they denigrate powerful mages (who must necessarily exercise potent Will)? Why would they look down their nose at someone whose Will is provably more true and potent than that of most Hermetics?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351283#post1351283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Chaos Magick is not symbolic, it is belief driven, so you might use symbolism or not. It include energy raising and directing and can accommodate almost any belief. So, it has energy, it has power in belief and is open enough. That's why I got it. Also, it is the glue that link the paradigm ro the instruments. The fact that consciousness (belief) afect realityusing energy. Together with the other practices I think it fits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do mean &quot;uses symbols&quot;. Austin Spare, the generally accepted grandfather of chaos magick, used sigils and writing as his Instruments. He did not believe in some system of occult symbolic logic or arcane correspondences (as a high ritualist might), but instead the sigils were improvisational and ad-hoc. In a Chaos magick sense, they were a way of portraying &quot;whatever it is I want to do, right now&quot;, in such a way as to help Spare focus his mind upon his objective. They were what helped him communicate his desire to the energies he thought would achieve it. Other chaos magicians such as Morrison come up with a &quot;representation for the task&quot; and focus upon that using mental energy, ranging from basic associations (&quot;this picture represents the me I want to be&quot; for a Life effect to change their shape) to elaborate fictional myths or pantheons (&quot;this story recreates my struggle against my addiction&quot; for a Mind effect to alleviate a drug habit, for example.) Socially-performative chaos magic tends, again, to posit causation and similarity between the desired effect and the actions of the mage (&quot;by transgressing this social boundary, I remove the shackles clouding my perception&quot; for a Spirit effect to see some other Realm or a Time effect to see the future.)<br /> <br /> While chaos magick is about the power of belief, it is most generally achieved by postulating some relationship as a scaffold for the mental energy to work with. The unusual trait of the Practice is the willingness to make up new scaffolds to suit an occasion and to scrap the scaffolding when it's over, and the insistence that no scaffold is in and of itself permanently powerful. The entry for Thought-Forms in M20 (pg 598) gets into this a bit, and the wiki page on chaos magic (or just Spare) isn't too bad as a start. (Spare himself seems to have thought getting fixated on a rigid occult system made your magic weaker, in fact. This is why M20's entry on the Practice talks about ditching instruments if they become &quot;too confining&quot;)<br /> <br /> This is what I mean about feeling like it's absent - I don't see any of the Practice's most common expressions. Do you have some other version of the practice in mind? I'm mostly a surface observer, so if there's some other expression of the philosophy you're using as inspiration, let me know.Raising and directing energy can be done Psionically (meditation, sheer willpower) or through Martial Arts (qi gong), so it just seems like a spare Practice for no good reason.<br /> <br /> My partner (who's better-read on Spare and chaos magic than I am) suggested automatic writing as part of the books Instrument - rather than <i>reading </i>a book about the subject the character wants to change, imagine them doing a lengthy free-association session where they write all the scientific and esoteric facts and factors surrounding what it is they want to achieve - for a Forces effect to control the weather, as much meteorological data as they can muster, and the time of day, and the wind direction, etc. etc. Rather than taking someone else's word for it, the character creates as clear a picture as possible (in his own words) for his mind to fixate on, so as to minimize the necessary energy to achieve the task - a very engineer-esque approach, and one which emphasizes the character's interest in scholarship and broad study. The more he knows about something, the easier it becomes to create a clear picture to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":1653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","user":"Five Eyes","date":". 11-28-2019, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T08:25:38-08:00","id":1351481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351427#post1351427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough.<br /> <br /> As to your proposed Chorister convert - the Order has not, historically, been particularly hesitant to insult mages from other Traditions. Remember, &quot;<i>What mage in any rival Tradition, of whatever skill, can boast the comprehensive knowledge of our least Adept?</i>&quot; Do you think the Order believes a Dreamspeaker or Technocrat, &quot;of whatever skill&quot;, knows the first thing about how magick actually works? If a Chorister has been using inadequate magic - little better than the theurgia taught to apprentices - their entire life, don't you need to start from the basics before you can teach them how to do it right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Order is very full of themselves, which I like. I believe that, and we're on the realm of opinions here, that it depends on the particular mage that is going to affiliate the Order. If he's going to the Order it's because he has at least some of their traits/beliefs. A Chorister that has absolutely nothing in common to the Order would probably not be accepted. <br /> Now, if he shares some beliefs (maybe angels and demons) and traits (determined,studious) he is going to need just some lessons. The more important thing is how he approach magick. The Chorister would have to lose the begging prayers style and adopt a more passive behavior. The mindset is more important than the instruments. <br /> So, to answer your question, the ammount of training will depend on the ammount of similarity to the Order that the mage has.<br /> Nevertheless no Awakened mage would go full training as if a sleeper. If the mage shares 0 traits/belief with the Order he would need to go from the basics (still no goetia nor theurgia though), but would probably bot be accepted. <br /> This is not the case of this char, that share all the Hermetic mindset and sone instruments. So, I can only deduce that he would receive lessons of the topic I already posted.<br /> <br /> [/quote]<br /> Why is your example for &quot;non-traditional&quot; Hermetic approaches someone trained in another Tradition altogether and grandfathered in (and even then, she's still an Alchemist!)?<br /> Why is your example for non-symbolic, non-religious mages a guy who explicitly finds Hermetic ritualism comforting and compatible with his Catholic upbringing?<br /> These seem like odd choices?[/quote]<br /> <br /> They are examples that the Order is not that rigid about focus. Livia cam from another Tradition and had a more scientific view of her magick, she is more into chemistry than alchemy. She underst the &quot;old art of spiritual transformation&quot; as &quot;science of consciousness altering substances&quot;. Just like my mage could see the use of the fifth pentacle of seven moons as nothing more than energy working, psionic effect.<br /> My point here is that the Order is not that rigid and every Hermetic in it has their own beliefs, which may even be scientific.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I hold Hermetic Will to be a subset of the Will exercised by all other mages. Compare their criteria for Will to that exercised by other mages - and remember, their criticism isn't that other mages refuse to acknowledge their own Will as the source of power. They say other mages are ill-trained, slavish blunderers - that they're technically, academically, and spiritually backwards. That they beg and plead and surrender their wills to forces outside of themselves. How can servility be Willful? And if it is Willful - then why would the Hermetics, who exult Will above all, sneer at it? If it works, it must be true Will, and yet the Order thinks otherwise. If they had a genuine understanding of what true Will was, why would they denigrate powerful mages (who must necessarily exercise potent Will)? Why would they look down their nose at someone whose Will is provably more true and potent than that of most Hermetics? </div> </div> </div>I see. You are right that other Traditions work in a different way and that affect how they use Will.<br /> However those characteristics (focused, energetic, forceful,etc) are not exclusive to Hermetics. While in general they do have them and other Trads don't, this doesn't means that particular mages cannot have it.<br /> This is one more reason why my mage would join the Order. They would see that his use of Will is pretty much the same as theirs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While chaos magick is about the power of belief, it is most generally achieved by postulating some relationship as a scaffold for the mental energy to work with. The unusual trait of the Practice is the willingness to make up new scaffolds to suit an occasion and to scrap the scaffolding when it's over, and the insistence that no scaffold is in and of itself permanently powerful. The entry for Thought-Forms in M20 (pg 598) gets into this a bit, and the wiki page on chaos magic (or just Spare) isn't too bad as a start. (Spare himself seems to have thought getting fixated on a rigid occult system made your magic weaker, in fact. This is why M20's entry on the Practice talks about ditching instruments if they become &quot;too confining&quot;)<br /> <br /> This is what I mean about feeling like it's absent - I don't see any of the Practice's most common expressions. Do you have some other version of the practice in mind? I'm mostly a surface observer, so if there's some other expression of the philosophy you're using as inspiration, let me know.Raising and directing energy can be done Psionically (meditation, sheer willpower) or through Martial Arts (qi gong), so it just seems like a spare Practice for no good reason. </div> </div> </div>I know a little about RL Chaos Magick and I see it as &quot;use what fits&quot; as long as you believe it. Not necessarily ditching instruments. So, if it's not a known classic usage of magick it could fit Chaos Magick. <br /> I added it because I likr Chaos Magick principles, it is very practical and my char do have this practical touch. Also it is related to power in belief instead of in instruments, which also fits. I see that I'm using it more because of his paradigm than his instruments. <br /> I understand your point, though, and would like suggestions on how to add it to the instruments as listed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My partner (who's better-read on Spare and chaos magic than I am) suggested automatic writing as part of the books Instrument - rather than <i>reading </i>a book about the subject the character wants to change, imagine them doing a lengthy free-association session where they write all the scientific and esoteric facts and factors surrounding what it is they want to achieve - for a Forces effect to control the weather, as much meteorological data as they can muster, and the time of day, and the wind direction, etc. etc. Rather than taking someone else's word for it, the character creates as clear a picture as possible (in his own words) for his mind to fixate on, so as to minimize the necessary energy to achieve the task - a very engineer-esque approach, and one which emphasizes the character's interest in scholarship and broad study. The more he knows about something, the easier it becomes to create a clear picture to work with. </div> </div> </div> What you mean by automatic writing?<br /> <br /> I loved the idea! I was thinking in adding study as part of Books/Scrolls/Periodics instruments and your explanation fitted perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T16:45:53-08:00","id":1351558,"title":"","content":"I sometimes have trouble following all the details of this discussion (my contribution was basically \u201cYou should think about how often he hooks up\u201d), but I\u2019m really impressed by how much you guys know about the metaphysical aspects of the game. Not being snarky; 100% sincere.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3153_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3153\" data-vbnamecard=\"3153\">Lord Revan</a> good luck with your character. Let me know how your first game goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T01:14:24-08:00","id":1351612,"title":"","content":"I <i>think </i>the reason they mentioned automatic writing specifically was because Spare intended his sigils - the writings he used to focus his desire - to touch his unconscious, rather than conscious mind (He thought the conscious mind couldn't achieve magic, basically.) So the equivalent practice with writing out a text would want to do so with a &quot;stream-of-consciousness&quot; approach, as if the character was freely associating between the various facts they know and ideas they have about a subject, instead of trying to create a rigid, orderly summary of their findings. The goal, after all, isn't to create a document for other people to read, but rather a comprehensive and detailed summary of what the desired spell/effect means to the character themselves. Imagine the difference between writing a detailed description of lightning versus trying to create a document that expresses the idea of Lightning so clearly it lets a mage control Forces.<br /> <br /> Not sure about other ways to link the Chaos practice without changing the list of Instruments (although I guess the proposed idea would swap out Books in favor of Writing). Maybe some of the Devices the character used during their transitional period (from between when they realized the energy could be directed by humans and the point where they ditched the Instrument) could be tied to it? Metronomes or white noise generators to help with entering a meditative state? I think the issue would be making it clear that the character doesn't use devices to <i>do stuff </i>but rather to help him <i>focus on the stuff his Consciousness is doing.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T14:21:12-08:00","id":1351913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five Eyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351612#post1351612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>think </i>the reason they mentioned automatic writing specifically was because Spare intended his sigils - the writings he used to focus his desire - to touch his unconscious, rather than conscious mind (He thought the conscious mind couldn't achieve magic, basically.) So the equivalent practice with writing out a text would want to do so with a &quot;stream-of-consciousness&quot; approach, as if the character was freely associating between the various facts they know and ideas they have about a subject, instead of trying to create a rigid, orderly summary of their findings. The goal, after all, isn't to create a document for other people to read, but rather a comprehensive and detailed summary of what the desired spell/effect means to the character themselves. Imagine the difference between writing a detailed description of lightning versus trying to create a document that expresses the idea of Lightning so clearly it lets a mage control Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are quite similar. You mean someting more like a sketch notebook with ideas/equations instead of writing an academic book? I prefer to keep books instead writing and add this &quot;study&quot; as part of the instrument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure about other ways to link the Chaos practice without changing the list of Instruments (although I guess the proposed idea would swap out Books in favor of Writing). Maybe some of the Devices the character used during their transitional period (from between when they realized the energy could be directed by humans and the point where they ditched the Instrument) could be tied to it? Metronomes or white noise generators to help with entering a meditative state? I think the issue would be making it clear that the character doesn't use devices to <i>do stuff </i>but rather to help him <i>focus on the stuff his Consciousness is doing.</i> </div> </div> </div>I see. Could an Etherite (or even technocrat) use Chaos Magick? how would that be?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T20:07:53-08:00","id":1351954,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to put a massive disclaimer upfront that despite my years and years of fascination with Ascension, I have no actual experience with playing it whatsoever. I have, however, wanted to combine Science with mystic paradigms before. (I keep coming back to the idea of using computer programs to run simulations of complex rituals, in particular.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351913#post1351913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. Could an Etherite (or even technocrat) use Chaos Magick? how would that be?</div> </div> </div> </div>An Etherite take on Chaos Magic may have potential in one staple of the Mad Scientist archetype, lab accidents that create amazing results but can't be exactly duplicated. The scientist knocks over a piece of lab equipment, uses the wrong chemical solution, or else something breaks in a surprisingly convenient way. It could also manifest as a 'What if I do this?' attitude where the mage ignores various safety protocols in favor is jumping into unplanned experiments on a whim and seeing what happens.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union... frowns upon doing either of those things. Especially since consistent, repeatable results are a central part of their version of science. That doesn't entirely rule out <i>some</i> form of it, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T11:07:41-08:00","id":1352035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351954#post1351954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Etherite take on Chaos Magic may have potential in one staple of the Mad Scientist archetype, lab accidents that create amazing results but can't be exactly duplicated. The scientist knocks over a piece of lab equipment, uses the wrong chemical solution, or else something breaks in a surprisingly convenient way. It could also manifest as a 'What if I do this?' attitude where the mage ignores various safety protocols in favor is jumping into unplanned experiments on a whim and seeing what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's howeverrrrr not quite what Chaos Magick *is* though. Chaos Magick is not just randomness or accidents, despite the probably misleading name.<br /> <br /> Chaos Magick is, in a way, the magical equivalent of Bruce Lee's Jeet Kun Do - in one way how it just lets you pick 'whatever works for you' in your magical pursuits, but also in another way where it does not stick to any tradition or fixed 'rules' - for Chaotes, the goal and result are what's important.<br /> Ironically Chaos Magick is very Purple Paradigm in the way that &quot;Nothing is true, everything is allowed&quot; and the notion of there being no objective truths but only one's belief are literally cornerstones of the practice. But in a fit of turning itself inside-out, several practices of Chaos Magick (usually involving Sigils) actually work by firmly implanting one's intent and will into a sigil - and then doing everything they can to actually forget what the sigil was about in the first place, in order to let the unoccupied mind do its will.<br /> <br /> Chaos Magick is also very self-paradoxial in the way that the goal is more important than how to get there. Some writings of Chaos Magick advice one, for example, in order to perform a certain belief's ritual as a tool, to *actually* acquire that belief over time. Then perform the rituals interent with it to reach your goal. And then to abandon that belief again for another. If that sounds weird to you, welcome to chaos magick.<br /> Other famous writers regarding the practice recommend letting go of any previous beliefs altogether, seeing any established dogma - religion and science - as a hindrance. One might jump in to say &quot;That's so Etherite&quot; but..no, it isn't, as Etherites actually work on establishing their own fixed dogma and theories - something that runs contrary to most Chaos Magick. We don't even need to mention Technocrats.<br /> <br /> So yeah, welcome to chaos magick. It's paradoxial-in-itself, it is very purple paradigm while advising to dive head-deep into paradigms you want to use as tools, while also advising to just come up with things of your own, and sometimes writers actually contradict each other while also acknowledging each other. Io Chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 12-02-2019, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T11:56:48-08:00","id":1352041,"title":"","content":"Ahh. Sorry for the misunderstanding, then. I'll back out of this conversation for now. (And maybe check out books from a more recent edition.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":2598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","user":"Gryphon's Feather","date":". 12-01-2019, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T20:02:08-08:00","id":1352097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1351913#post1351913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could an Etherite (or even technocrat) use Chaos Magick? how would that be?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's certainly possible for a technomancer, most often paired with a belief in psychic phenomenon (most obviously, the Psionics Practice.) A technomantic approach could accept the terms used by chaos magicians - there is some form of mental energy which ritual action can tap into - or adopt some of their methods (audio playback, repetitive mantras), as chaos magicians tend to express these in stripped-down or pseudo-scientific terms. Magical approaches based on archetypes would, I think, be less common, except for mages who have dots in Spirit.<br /> <br /> The Union would take a dim view on the Practice, but it can be reconciled with Tychoidean cosmology fairly well. We might also imagine a Syndicate character who, all things considered, believes in luck, and (being a technocrat), explores the most &quot;practical&quot; and &quot;rational&quot; ritual approach to try and control luck. These would both be ideological outliers, and it's the sort of thing which would keep them from getting promoted - or, in a more severe case, they'd be Conditioned until they renounced their &quot;superstitious&quot; approach. Still, it's in the limits of what you'd expect for a Technocrat PC, as they tend to be more &quot;out there&quot; than the average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T05:19:22-08:00","id":1352144,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> excellent description of the practice!<br /> Note how it is kinda opposite to the classical Hermetic HR user (full of fixed meanings and rigid rules) stereotype, and yet it is in their used practices list.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1653_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1653\" data-vbnamecard=\"1653\">Five Eyes</a>, I can see that this is a very open practice, that almost anyone could use or adapt to their paradigm.<br /> Like Ambrosia said, it is completely related to the belief in beliefs (Nothing is true, everything is permitted) and I see that it fits nicely in the char paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T11:48:00-08:00","id":1352189,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Lord Revan;n1351190]<br /> So, I guess this is explained enough. I would love to see your opinions about it and am willing to makes changes. But I wouldn't like to change the focus list<br /> [QUOTE]<br /> <br /> <u>Paradigm:</u><br /> So, he doesn't believe in any of the principles of sleeper science, all that he was taugth in engineering it's a lie because the universe it's just wish fulfillment of the strong, it has no laws nor logic....yet he's an engineer (proud to be) that uses that very logical scientific approach in his day to day life. I don't buy it.<br /> <br /> I think that if you believe in actual natural laws, even if these are not the laws of magick, then you believe in something less formless than chaos and will ruling the universe...either the cosmos it's &quot;mechanisistic&quot; (not in the RL sense, but as the Paradigm describes it, a place with fundamental laws that rule it), or it's ruled by Wills more powerful than your own (Gods and Monsters + Migth) that set those laws...or something, anything, that would give space to the laws of nature to exist out there and be more or less consistent from person to person. Otherwise ALL you learned in engineering it's, best case scenario, true by virtue of you wanting it to be true, and could be false tomorrow...and then how could you know that magick it's not scientific?. Sicence it's not scientific for this guy<br /> <br /> <u>Practice/Instruments:</u><br /> This is largely ok, new-agey stuff that could fit on any Tradition.<br /> <br /> I don't get how Machines tapped into any of this to cause magick happen, though. Other than enhancing your own body/mind, since all the power seems to come from there<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Knowledge is power and books is all about knowledge. He likes to study both sleeper science and magickal theory. <b>Magickal theory is how magick behaves, how Paradox and Quintessence works, what and how Consensus works, etc.</b> </div> </div> </div>So, he likes to read <i>Mage: The Ascension</i> rulebooks? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Call me crazy, but I have the distinct impression that IOC books are going to be more than filled with all that symbolism and/or weird theories he doesn't like, while having very little, and probably contradictory, data about that subject you mentioned...<br /> <br /> Really, that way of presenting this Instrument it's <i>bad</i>. It's almost insta-ban for any Concept right there, not just<i> Five Eyes </i>would be suspicious.<br /> <br /> NEVER say that &quot;magickal theory&quot; it's about rules. Magickal theory in Mage <i>always </i>talks about how mages &quot;belive&quot; magick works, which usually has a lot more to do with the how the Paradigms/Practices define magick. It would be better to just say that he likes to read about his brand of magick (or others, to adapt them), otherwise it reads like you want your character to know the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Devices/Machines</b>: One of his first instruments used to tap the energy. At first he used simple yet efficient devices like coils, receivers, modulators to raise and diret the energy the way he wanted. With time, he understood that he was affecting the machines output by himself and they were mere instruments to help him in this. He began using more rudimentary devices, involving crystals coupled with wires in their interior to gather the energy. He began using them less and less to the point that eventually he stopped using them altogether (dropped instrument). It is important to note that this was an initial stage, he didn't relied on them for long and they was very, very rudimentar and simple. <b>He didn't quite understood yet the mysteries of the energy and was trying to use science and technology to get a result. When he realised the mystical aspect that that energy had, he stopped trying to explain it that way. </b>I'd say that all kind of effects could be done this way, it is just a matter of using the right device in the right way. After dropping this instrument, he might use them more like a totem of his Awakened Will than a device per se. </div> </div> </div>Rather than surpassing Machines, this sounds more like he changed his Practice. He was practicing &quot;science stuff&quot; to alter reality (and it worked, because he was already Awakened) and latter he ceased to do this science and started to apply a different approach. It's not just that he &quot;doesn't need machines anymore&quot;, the way these could be used as Instrument it's going to have completely different implications compared with the time before he surpassed them (he didn't understood the mysteries, he was *wrong* about the nature of magick back then).<br /> <br /> I'm not very clear about what happens with the Instruments when you abandon a Practice. I don't think you can keep using them. It would be less contentious, I think, to have machines that build up on how this character sees magick *now* rather than an aftertougth that &quot;didn't work as intended&quot;, regarded as ignorance<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, why would the Order of Hermes be intersted on him?<br /> He is an aggressive, determined <b>mage</b>. He probably awoke by himself and began his mage life as an Orphan, later joining the Order. He share the Order's foundations and some beliefs, he is definitely a Traditional and is bold, cocky, power/knowledge-hungry House Flambeau would be the place for him. He has heavy knowledge of the forces of nature and is very fond of electricity (and vulgar magick). He would be seen as a very great weapon in the war against Technocracy, even that he doesn't completely fit the Order stereotype.<br /> <br /> And why would the Etherites want him?<br /> He is an engineer and has a scientifical mind. He is always seeking knowledge and is very dedicated. That is enough for them to have him there, even that only to learn more with him. Many would see him as a farse, or even a joke because of his beliefs. Calling himself a mage and believeing that everything the Tradition do is magick do not help his case. While he might fit this Tradition, that's not the feel I want to this char... </div> </div> </div>Etherites also are at war against Technocracy, and are bold, cocky and power/knowledge-hungry...I think the main conceit should be the aesthetics (where does he stands in the pointy-hat vs lab-coat debate) that he will use.<br /> <br /> The way you talk about this it's still very open. As Five Eyes said, feels more of a psychic that would use &quot;powers&quot; than a magician who would cast actual &quot;spells&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-02-2019, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-03T06:01:04-08:00","id":1352344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1352189#post1352189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u>Paradigm:</u><br /> So, he doesn't believe in any of the principles of sleeper science, all that he was taugth in engineering it's a lie because the universe it's just wish fulfillment of the strong, it has no laws nor logic....yet he's an engineer (proud to be) that uses that very logical scientific approach in his day to day life. I don't buy it.<br /> I think that if you believe in actual natural laws, even if these are not the laws of magick, then you believe in something less formless than chaos and will ruling the universe...either the cosmos it's &amp;quot;mechanisistic&amp;quot; (not in the RL sense, but as the Paradigm describes it, a place with fundamental laws that rule it), or it's ruled by Wills more powerful than your own (Gods and Monsters + Migth) that set those laws...or something, anything, that would give space to the laws of nature to exist out there and be more or less consistent from person to person. Otherwise ALL you learned in engineering it's, best case scenario, true by virtue of you wanting it to be true, and could be false tomorrow...and then how could you know that magick it's not scientific?. Sicence it's not scientific for this guy</div> </div> </div> </div>He do believe in sleeper science principles. I made that very clear. He is a proud engineer and he doesn't believe the universe i wish fulfilment of the strong. He just believes that consciousness, Will, etc. is able to affect reality, to change it. The laws of physics all work as he knows, except when some enlightened mind do something to bend them.<br /> He do not believe Reality itself is created by Chaos or Consciousness. Just that it can be shaped by them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't get how Machines tapped into any of this to cause magick happen, though. Other than enhancing your own body/mind, since all the power seems to come from there </div> </div> </div>All the magick comes from energy, which were tapped by the devices. This energy is directed/manipulated by consciousness, but he tougth initially that only machines could manipulate this energy (like any skeptic would believe). Later he discovered that he can do that with more esoteric ways.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, he likes to read <i>Mage: The Ascension</i> rulebooks? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Call me crazy, but I have the distinct impression that IOC books are going to be more than filled with all that symbolism and/or weird theories he doesn't like, while having very little, and probably contradictory, data about that subject you mentioned...<br /> Really, that way of presenting this Instrument it's <i>bad</i>. It's almost insta-ban for any Concept right there, not just<i> Five Eyes </i>would be suspicious.<br /> <br /> NEVER say that &amp;quot;magickal theory&amp;quot; it's about rules. Magickal theory in Mage <i>always </i>talks about how mages &amp;quot;belive&amp;quot; magick works, which usually has a lot more to do with the how the Paradigms/Practices define magick. It would be better to just say that he likes to read about his brand of magick (or others, to adapt them), otherwise it reads like you want your character to know the rules </div> </div> </div>No. Paradox, Quintessence and Concensus are terms known and used in-game (sometimes with other names, depending on Tradition). They can be studied in-game and we even have revised books with stories where characters talk about them.<br /> And even if he gets a book full of symbolism from an Hermetic library he can still take the meaning of it, seeing behind all the symbolism. Having said that he would probably choose carefully what he would read, searching from both science books for inspiration in his effects and magickal tomes for discovering more about magick. <br /> Using books together with study is a very cool way to fit all this into the character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Rather than surpassing Machines, this sounds more like he changed his Practice. He was practicing &amp;quot;science stuff&amp;quot; to alter reality (and it worked, because he was already Awakened) and latter he ceased to do this science and started to apply a different approach. It's not just that he &amp;quot;doesn't need machines anymore&amp;quot;, the way these could be used as Instrument it's going to have completely different implications compared with the time before he surpassed them (he didn't understood the mysteries, he was *wrong* about the nature of magick back then).<br /> <br /> I'm not very clear about what happens with the Instruments when you abandon a Practice. I don't think you can keep using them. It would be less contentious, I think, to have machines that build up on how this character sees magick *now* rather than an aftertougth that &amp;quot;didn't work as intended&amp;quot;, regarded as ignorance </div> </div> </div>He wasn't wrong, machines can manipulated that energy. He just discovered other ways to do it.<br /> I wouldn't say he changed practices. I would say that his awakening happened in a process and when he fully Awakened he had all those instruments, realising that he couldbuse his body. After some time he felt that his body was a more efficient way to direct the energy and stopped using devices altogether. Now, he just use them when he wants to add more juice into his spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Etherites also are at war against Technocracy, and are bold, cocky and power/knowledge-hungry...I think the main conceit should be the aesthetics (where does he stands in the pointy-hat vs lab-coat debate) that he will use.<br /> <br /> The way you talk about this it's still very open. As Five Eyes said, feels more of a psychic that would use &amp;quot;powers&amp;quot; than a magician who would cast actual &amp;quot;spells&amp;quot;. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. What I am looking for is a &quot;pointy-hat&quot; that work with energy. Think of something like MCU Dr. Strange, but instead of a surgeon, he was an engineer. And he uses more of his past knowledge in his spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T06:55:27-08:00","id":1353000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1352344#post1352344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He do believe in sleeper science principles. I made that very clear. He is a proud engineer and he doesn't believe the universe i wish fulfilment of the strong. He just believes that consciousness, Will, etc. is able to affect reality, to change it. The laws of physics all work as he knows, except when some enlightened mind do something to bend them.<br /> He do not believe Reality itself is created by Chaos or Consciousness. Just that it can be shaped by them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this wasn't very precise: &quot;<i>basically, he believes that Reality is unknown and changeable, product of our own beliefs.&quot; ...</i>And that's exactly why I don't buy that he believes in the Paradigm you mentioned.<br /> <br /> Paradigm it's not a mere excuse to cast spells: As M20 puts it: &quot;Mage paradigms represent the various belief systems that Awakened and unAwakened people use to understand the world they share&quot;<br /> <br /> He, explicitly, doesn't believe that &quot;Everything is Chaos&quot;...he believes very few things are Chaos...and the others you've mentioned just &quot;inform&quot; that one. Imagine a dude that believes in God granting him milacres, but then denying God himself had a say on how the universe works...that would beg the question of how do his spells work. And that it's the question Paradigm should answer<br /> <br /> By the descriptions you made, it's most likely that he believes in a variant of<i> Tech Holds All the Answers: </i> He believes in an universe that has scientific laws that make it work the way it works. It's just that this universe harbors magical laws alongside the natural ones, that interact under special circumnstanced and can't be understood by science for some reason (perhaps that's where a limited version of Chaos enters).<br /> That he tries to apply experiments to understand magick and sepparate the &quot;wheat from the chaf&quot; only proves that he believes the universe in general, and magick in particular, &quot;is rational and understandable&quot;, even if magick itself can't be replicated the way propper science would want<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't say he changed practices. I would say that his awakening happened in a process and when he fully Awakened he had all those instruments, realising that he couldbuse his body. After some time he felt that his body was a more efficient way to direct the energy and stopped using devices altogether. Now, he just use them when he wants to add more juice into his spells. </div> </div> </div>Ok, I can see this working as not having full understanding of the Practice yet.<br /> <br /> It's a bit odd. Surpassing instruments it's not described as discovering these aren't efficient, and throwing them aside, but as understanding that they're not <i>necessary (</i>in fact, that these provide a bonus it's easy to understand as a testament to their efficiency).<br /> More so, mages usually know their Instruments are among the many tools that the Practice/s provide. If the mage thinks an instrument he internalized it's &quot;bad&quot; for some reason, 99% of the time makes more sense to discard it and learn a better Instrument of the same Practice, rather than to eternize it's concept as a surpass...But I could see this as an aspect of his Practice struggling with his past life. Like, he really <i>wants </i>machines to be able to replicate what humans do, even if his esoterical understanding points they can't be that good at it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No. Paradox, Quintessence and Concensus are terms known and used in-game (sometimes with other names, depending on Tradition). They can be studied in-game and we even have revised books with stories where characters talk about them.<br /> And even if he gets a book full of symbolism from an Hermetic library he can still take the meaning of it, seeing behind all the symbolism. </div> </div> </div>I concede that you can find books about those subjects. There are mages dedicated to study Paradox, and the other stuff, and thus there are books about that.<br /> <br /> But you miss my point, what I think it's <i>bad</i> it's to regard the rules as the magick theory your mage will study/care about, disregarding the rest.<br /> <br /> Books about &quot;magick theory&quot; are written &quot;in character&quot; by people<i> that believe their arcane symbols are very much part of that magic theory</i>. It's extremely artificial to say that you will disregard the parts of that magic theory that don't correspond directly with the rules. I don't think ANY mage (much less any Hermetic) would believe &quot;magical theory&quot; it's what you said. Oh, it covers that, sure...and then a hundred subjects more your character apparently cares little about.<br /> <br /> When a Chaos Magician talks about researching magick theory...he may believe Crowley books could be on the menu. But apparently your's a chaos magician that doesn't care much about chaos magick. No, no. Give me the books about Paradox, the Consensus, <i>real stuff. </i>Then he sees behind the veil of symbolism <i>that the authors honestly believed to be realy magickal</i> into what he <i>knows </i>it's <i>the real magick theory</i>?\u200b<br /> <br /> I'm not against Hermetic characters researching, say, Paradox (altrough I would remind the players that researching this isn't the same as knowing the rules by dice/dot)...I'm against Hermetic characters declaring that they're interested in books about Paradox, but care little about the actual Hermetic theory and the esoteric.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having said that he would probably choose carefully what he would read, searching from both science books for inspiration in his effects and magickal tomes for discovering more about magick.<br /> Using books together with study is a very cool way to fit all this into the character. </div> </div> </div>I think it could be cool, if it was phrased different. You say your character it's a very wizardly wizard...yet he's ver specific about being interested only in stuff that also exists in the rules. Stuff that's useful, but says nothing about the kind of gestures your mage will use, the kind of spells he will manifest trough his reading, the kind of machines he will build...and it's THAT, not the rules, what will make your mage feel like a mystic (or not)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Indeed. What I am looking for is a &quot;pointy-hat&quot; that work with energy. Think of something like MCU Dr. Strange, but instead of a surgeon, he was an engineer. And he uses more of his past knowledge in his spells. </div> </div> </div>Well, then we're back to: Dr. Strange dresses the part.<br /> <br /> Note that while Dr. Strange have some &quot;quantum-physic&quot; explanations about some stuff (mostly given by the Ancient), it's the rich magical world (with magical amulets, esoteric runes and ancient grimoires) where he learns and practices his stuff what makes he &quot;feel&quot; like a magician instead of a mutant like the MCU Scarlet Witch (that also does gestures and manipulates &quot;energy&quot;)<br /> <br /> I think you need to put more emphasis there. If you say he values &quot;arcane knowledge&quot;, but then say that this knowledge it's the rules of Mage and your chartacter would shit on the Emerald Table...I'm left knowing nothing about how your magick looks. Nothing in the description of the Focus shows any particular interest in the mystical, other than the fact he believes to be a mystic and calls what he does &quot;magic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-06-2019, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T14:19:33-08:00","id":1353146,"title":"","content":"First of all, thanks for all the constructive coments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1349104-scientific-mystic?p=1353000#post1353000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, this wasn't very precise: &amp;quot;<i>basically, he believes that Reality is unknown and changeable, product of our own beliefs.&amp;quot; ...</i>And that's exactly why I don't buy that he believes in the Paradigm you mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wasn\u2019t clear. The product is the change. So the universe can exist without life. But only consciousness can shape it like mages do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradigm it's not a mere excuse to cast spells: As M20 puts it: &amp;quot;Mage paradigms represent the various belief systems that Awakened and unAwakened people use to understand the world they share&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> He, explicitly, doesn't believe that &amp;quot;Everything is Chaos&amp;quot;...he believes very few things are Chaos...and the others you've mentioned just &amp;quot;inform&amp;quot; that one. Imagine a dude that believes in God granting him milacres, but then denying God himself had a say on how the universe works...that would beg the question of how do his spells work. And that it's the question Paradigm should answer </div> </div> </div>Nowehere is said that the mage must believe exactly as is said in the paradigm text. And even if that were the case, Evertything is Chaos do not state that Reality is created by human minds. The Chaos of his paradigms comes from the uncertainty that the enlightened mind can generate. The universe can be twisted like a \u201cEtch-a-Sketch\u201d by those who understand that using energy.<br /> In your example, the guy can believe God grants him miracles and yet did not created (or is not) the whole universe. I don\u00b4t see your point, really.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By the descriptions you made, it's most likely that he believes in a variant of<i> Tech Holds All the Answers: </i> He believes in an universe that has scientific laws that make it work the way it works. It's just that this universe harbors magical laws alongside the natural ones, that interact under special circumnstanced and can't be understood by science for some reason (perhaps that's where a limited version of Chaos enters).<br /> That he tries to apply experiments to understand magick and sepparate the &amp;quot;wheat from the chaf&amp;quot; only proves that he believes the universe in general, and magick in particular, &amp;quot;is rational and understandable&amp;quot;, even if magick itself can't be replicated the way propper science would want </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u00b4t say that. Magick is exactly the only thing that he do not find rational and understandable, even though he tried to (understand). \u201cTech holds all answers\u201d also consider \u201cmagick as a science that hasn\u00b4t yet been accepted by the average person\u201d, but the char itself do not consider it part of science. Also, he do not realies so much in Tech, only 1 of his instruments use tech.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, I can see this working as not having full understanding of the Practice yet.<br /> <br /> It's a bit odd. Surpassing instruments it's not described as discovering these aren't efficient, and throwing them aside, but as understanding that they're not <i>necessary (</i>in fact, that these provide a bonus it's easy to understand as a testament to their efficiency).<br /> More so, mages usually know their Instruments are among the many tools that the Practice/s provide. If the mage thinks an instrument he internalized it's &amp;quot;bad&amp;quot; for some reason, 99% of the time makes more sense to discard it and learn a better Instrument of the same Practice, rather than to eternize it's concept as a surpass... </div> </div> </div>I see. I could see the char thinking they are not necessary anymore. \u201cefficient\u201d an \u201cnecessary\u201d could be changed here.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I could see this as an aspect of his Practice struggling with his past life. Like, he really <i>wants </i>machines to be able to replicate what humans do, even if his esoterical understanding points they can't be that good at it. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. He do struggle with his sleeper knowledge. That\u2019s a central point of the char. He is a skeptical engineer that awakened and had to adapt his beliefs and knowledges. About the efficiency of machines vs. body, I don\u2019t know which would be better. But he definitely knows that machines are not needed anymore.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I concede that you can find books about those subjects. There are mages dedicated to study Paradox, and the other stuff, and thus there are books about that.<br /> <br /> But you miss my point, what I think it's <i>bad</i> it's to regard the rules as the magick theory your mage will study/care about, disregarding the rest.<br /> <br /> Books about &amp;quot;magick theory&amp;quot; are written &amp;quot;in character&amp;quot; by people<i> that believe their arcane symbols are very much part of that magic theory</i>. It's extremely artificial to say that you will disregard the parts of that magic theory that don't correspond directly with the rules. I don't think ANY mage (much less any Hermetic) would believe &amp;quot;magical theory&amp;quot; it's what you said. Oh, it covers that, sure...and then a hundred subjects more your character apparently cares little about.<br /> <br /> When a Chaos Magician talks about researching magick theory...he may believe Crowley books could be on the menu. But apparently your's a chaos magician that doesn't care much about chaos magick. No, no. Give me the books about Paradox, the Consensus, <i>real stuff. </i>Then he sees behind the veil of symbolism <i>that the authors honestly believed to be realy magickal</i> into what he <i>knows </i>it's <i>the real magick theory</i>?<br /> <br /> I'm not against Hermetic characters researching, say, Paradox (altrough I would remind the players that researching this isn't the same as knowing the rules by dice/dot)...I'm against Hermetic characters declaring that they're interested in books about Paradox, but care little about the actual Hermetic theory and the esoteric. </div> </div> </div>I see your point. Yes, the mage wouldn\u2019t be able to separate \u201crules\u201d magickal study and \u201cfluff\u201d magicka study and he probably would study both. However, this doesn\u2019t mean that he can\u2019t select what he will study, according to his paradigm. So, esoteric things regarding consciousness, mind, Will, energy, dimensions, etc. would interest him (together with concepts like Consensus,Paradox,etc.). Books of deities, symbols, religions, etc. wouldn\u2019t. He might still study them through his lens, much like Livia in Trad book does, though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it could be cool, if it was phrased different. You say your character it's a very wizardly wizard...yet he's ver specific about being interested only in stuff that also exists in the rules. Stuff that's useful, but says nothing about the kind of gestures your mage will use, the kind of spells he will manifest trough his reading, the kind of machines he will build...and it's THAT, not the rules, what will make your mage feel like a mystic (or not) </div> </div> </div>What you mean? I posted examples of use of the instruments. The base of them is energy manipulation. You mean exactly for an effect?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, then we're back to: Dr. Strange dresses the part.<br /> <br /> Note that while Dr. Strange have some &amp;quot;quantum-physic&amp;quot; explanations about some stuff (mostly given by the Ancient), it's the rich magical world (with magical amulets, esoteric runes and ancient grimoires) where he learns and practices his stuff what makes he &amp;quot;feel&amp;quot; like a magician instead of a mutant like the MCU Scarlet Witch (that also does gestures and manipulates &amp;quot;energy&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think you need to put more emphasis there. If you say he values &amp;quot;arcane knowledge&amp;quot;, but then say that this knowledge it's the rules of Mage and your chartacter would shit on the Emerald Table...I'm left knowing nothing about how your magick looks. Nothing in the description of the Focus shows any particular interest in the mystical, other than the fact he believes to be a mystic and calls what he does &amp;quot;magic&amp;quot;. </div> </div> </div>I see. I have no problems with ancient tomes, magical amulets,etc. The issue is with religion, invocations of entities, and power in the symbols. If the source of power can be allocated into the \u201cenergy\u201d he has no problem.<br /> I see the power in belief and consciousness along with a mysterious energy as being very mystical. It only get scientific if you can explain all this crazyness with equations and math.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"http